{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/431083-101-scion-story-hooks","id":431083,"title":"101 Scion Story Hooks","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-06T23:13:31-08:00","id":431083,"title":"101 Scion Story Hooks","content":"<b>Meh... why not add one here? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>001)</b> Okay, sure, the old religions could get a little wild when it came to rituals and celebrations. But what happens when they take things a little bit too far? There is another hero in the city, who fancies themselves a future god of revelry. As far as killing Titan Spawn goes, they're pretty good at their job. But their method of celebrating is the pinacle of vulgarity. This hero's adoring fans launch themselves into orgies in full view of the public, with no regard for who or even what they're fornicating with. Alcohol flows among them until people are collapsing where they stand, sometimes in mid conversation! People dance until they are too sore to move, and sing until their voices give out. Those who manage to survive this extreme partying (some of them die from exhaustion) wake up in a daze with no memory of what transpired.<br /> <br /> You're band suspects they might have fallen victim to the Titan of Chaos, but beyond their ecstatic party throwing, you have little evidence to go on. If your suspicions are correct, it would be extremely dangerous to let this Scion advance in power. But if you're wrong, you run the risk of angering not only this Scion, but their extended family who supports them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>002)</b> Hephaestus needs to explain to his kids what constitutes as a joke! One of his Scions is a sewage worker, of all things. In a fit of boredom, they decided to convert the city's sewers into a labyrinth, complete with its own Minotaur! It may sound harmless enough to any heroes that choose to stay above ground, but the city workers have a job to do, and they can't fix the plumbing if they're dodging spring loaded buzz saws, fire breathing scorpions, or man sized bulls swinging an axe at their face! So before the entire city starts to smell like shit, it looks like you're going to have to climb down there and solve the problem!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>003)</b> There comes a time when you have to decide whether the old ways are better or not. You've just found out there's a scion, one of your own family, who's decided their heritage makes them superior to mortals. They're running a smuggling operation, kidnapping people and selling them into slavery over seas. The money they earn goes to furthering the Scion's fight against the Titans and building the glory of your family's name.<br /> <br /> So now the question is... where do your loyalties reside? Will you allow this smuggling operation to survive in order to increase your power, or will you put a stop to it and possibly anger your pantheon? Either way, you're going to lose respect, either for yourself or from your peers!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 03-22-2015, 08:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T18:10:26-07:00","id":449963,"title":"","content":"Aww, nobody has any?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T02:47:16-07:00","id":452445,"title":"","content":"<b>004) </b>The gods of the Dodekatheon decide, in a sudden jolt of competitive brotherhood and vanity to host a cross pantheon competition of sports and games. Some &quot;Olympic&quot; games, if you will. The varying pantheons have agreed to participate and will send their chosen Scions to compete in games testing the various attributes and strengths that exemplify them and their parentage. However, exactly what these games entail, and the risks involved haven't been entirely explained. But who cares! The winner gets respect and bragging rights with the other pantheons for all of eternity! Oh and maybe some cool birthrights and favors or something.<br /> <br /> <b>005)</b> The Scion of a powerful fertility god has come to you and your band asking for your assistance in destroying some titanspawn threatening their home. The titanspawn, masquerading as a lumber company are destroying the natural beauty of the world and attempting to corrupt it with more industry and technology, forcing humanity to forget and condemn the natural beauty of the world! Weird though, because all of those lumberjacks sure seem like regular humans who are just doing their jobs. And some of the fertility gods of other pantheons seem REALLY on board with this mission. Like more than they should for a mission supposedly brought by one of their rivals. Are we really the good guys here?<br /> <br /> <b>006)</b> A new human with the gift of prophecy has been identified. It is imperative that your pantheon &quot;gain custody&quot; of this powerful mortal. They must be located and extracted as soon as possible. So how do we find them? Wait, they're a social media sensation? Constantly broadcasting their location via chirper, speedygram, and picturebook? What does this post mean about &quot;the face of the night sky trembling and shedding tears of light as her heroes fall&quot;? Is that a titanspawn doing jello shots with them in Vegas...?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3653,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3653-thegraysoul","user":"TheGraySoul","date":". 03-22-2015, 05:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3653-thegraysoul","name":"TheGraySoul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T05:09:18-07:00","id":452532,"title":"","content":"(I chortle at the idea of Thor's children participating in the &quot;hammer&quot; toss)<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>007)</b> Vampires... considering everything else you've faced, these blood suckers should be like swatting flies. Except for this one, oddly enough... They fancy themselves as some kind of rising &quot;blood&quot; god and have been racking up a dangerously high magnitude of human sacrifices. Another Scion went in to clean up the problem... and didn't come back in one piece! Is this vampire really the Scion of some violent deity, or are they getting assistance from something else?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T00:13:30-07:00","id":453935,"title":"","content":"<b>008)</b> An agent of heaven has gone missing and the gods need you to find them. They managed to locate the general area of a city where this agent is located but couldn't get anymore specifics. The hard part starts once you find them though. In addition to protecting this agent from the Titanspawn that are no doubt hunting them, they seem to have contracted amnesia and are living life as an average mortal. How will you find them and convince them of who they really are? (Which is who again?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3653,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3653-thegraysoul","user":"TheGraySoul","date":". 07-04-2018, 02:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3653-thegraysoul","name":"TheGraySoul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-28T13:43:02-07:00","id":460383,"title":"","content":"Here are some from the old White Wolf Wiki - sorry that I don't know who actually came up with them...<br /> <br /> <b>009)</b> The Lost City: Some twenty to thirty years ago, the farming community of Bright Hill, located in rural (even by local standards) Montana, cut off all contact with the outside world. The last news anyone had out of the place was that a local farmer had unearthed some strange item plowing his field (confusing just about everyone as he'd plowed that same field the same way since he was fifteen and only found more and more dirt). The exact look and nature of the thing is a mystery, with every account colored by thirty years of tall tales and stranger occurrences seen off on the horizon. However, everyone agrees that the last thing anyone heard out of Bright Hill was that the town had, for some completely unknown reason, decided to pump every cent in the town treasury into building a Monorail. Exactly what they hoped to accomplish with the device is unknown. But about six months after the decision, a few people noticed that their friend in and around Bright Hill hadn't really been in touch lately. Three dozen died trying to drive into town. The survivors told horror stories about strange weapons that sprouted from the ground, roads that devoured cars, lightning arcing between distant towers and along the disturbing steel ring that surrounded the old downtown, suspended by unknown forces in mid-air. Who (or perhaps more likely &quot;what&quot;) caused this incredible change in the populace is unknown, and even attempts by the local National Guard resulted in nothing more than a field of casualties. The state and national government seem, strangely, unconcerned with any of this; in fact, the governor recently released a statement declaring the entire thing was likely an elaborate hoax, an opinion shared by thousands of others around the country who've heard the story of &quot;The Mechanical Ghost Town of Bright Hill&quot; around the same campfires as stories concerning the Jersey Devil or the Hook-hand killer.<br /> <br /> <b>010)</b> That which was left Behind: Most think that every Titan left when they broke free from their prison. That is unfortunately incorrect. Something still lurks in the deep, hidden places, hating everything blessed by the Gods. Whether they admit it or not, that's the reason the deepest caverns across the world have closed down their lowest levels. That's the reason that mining interests have been loosing money, having to pay out higher and higher bonuses for hazard pay. That's the reason you're being sent to the tourist trap known as Natural Bridge, Virginia and the deepest cavern on the east coast of the United States.<br /> <br /> <b>011) </b>The Fountain:In the course of the Scions travels, they come across a beautiful ornate fountain (perhaps the sky burst in a green haze and led them there, perhaps they stumbled upon it, not important either way). The fountain is made of a solid piece of gemstone (pick your favorite) and a cool, crisp, refreshing water flows from its many outlets. The basin itself if about 15 feet across and rises up for 4 tiers of ornate beauty. When someone drinks from the fountain (the water is perfectly safe by the way), the fountain issues forth a voice, asking those in its presence if they seek truth. Then asks if they seek knowledge, then asks if they seek understanding. If answered yes on all accounts, the Fountain then issues them a challenge. Finish a task, and they will have their answer. The fountain then emits a wave of arcane power that washes over the pcs. When they open their eyes, they're not feeling quite themselves. (At this point, shuffle the sheets around. Preferably for comedic potential). The Scions are stuck this way, literally walking a mile in each others shoes (or boots, or heels, or birkenstocks, or whatever...) until they finish their task (which can be whatever you want)<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1087-sylvanwulf","name":"Sylvanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-28T21:50:48-07:00","id":460679,"title":"","content":"<b>010)</b> It's terrible, absolutely terrible! Your Relic has been stolen and put up for display as a trophy for a pompous rival's party. If your father Thor hears about this, there's no telling how he'll react! You have a plan to sneak in and get your Relic back... but... well its going to require an impressive feat of disguise. Hey, if dear old Dad can do it, then surely you can too!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 03-31-2015, 08:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T13:11:07-07:00","id":463764,"title":"","content":"<b>013)</b> Old man /Kaggen, the Bushman Mantis god, creator and trickster, decided to go to sleep. The trouble is, his dreams tend to become reality. Even changing the natural order is not out of the question. Can you sneak into the dream of one of the oldest beings alive, and make sure that ticks dont become the dominant species or something?<br /> <br /> <b>014)</b> Dionysos is slowly going mad. And no, his usual persona is very sane compared to what is emerging. Kybele was able to cure him in the past, but the goddess does not accept visitors in her wilderness retreat. Do you persevere until she finally relents? Or do you take Ariadne`s advise, and head to Knossos to search for Asterion? Wait, Asterion and Dionysos are...<br /> <br /> <b>015)</b> Have you ever felt a longing for... Euripides? No matter, you will have to search for him anyway. Yes, in Hades. No, you are not allowed to question orders. Yes, judging a contest between furious tragic poets is part of the job. As well as preventing all those dead people from sneaking out to the world of the living in your luggage (but of course you have luggage!). You are only allowed to take Euripides with you. Or maybe Aeschylus is better? Unless, of course, those drama queens throttle you before a decision can be made.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5530-xanthias","name":"Xanthias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T20:41:56-07:00","id":469133,"title":"","content":"016) Ishtar just broke the fucking gates to the Underworld. There are dead Mesopotamians <i>everywhere.</i> Sort this nonsense out before things get out of hand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-05T05:40:08-07:00","id":469294,"title":"","content":"<b>017)</b> You're getting called out in front of everyone. A cult of mortals are declaring their god is the true faith, while your followers spout nothing but heresy and worship a false god. The mortals have set up a contest to see which god can perform the most feats and prove themselves worthy of their worship. If you fail the challenge, it could result in a significant drop in followers. So will you answer the challenge, or do the mortals need to be taught a lesson for insulting the gods in such blatant manner?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-05T12:02:54-07:00","id":469495,"title":"","content":"<b>018)</b> You happen to have met Tezcatlipoca`s Night Axe (Yoaltepoztli) headless manifestation, and passed the test (by taking his heart). Of course, now Tezcatlipoca is very interested in you. So have some more tests, weirdness and unnecessary danger. Is there a way to convince Necoc Yaotl to leave you be without angering the fickle god? Oh, and those three or four captives you were promised as a reward? You <i>must </i>capture and sacrifice them. Soon.<br /> <br /> <b> 019) </b>One of the tablets containing the laws of Ur-Nammu disappeared. You are charged by Utu with protecting the rest, since the Titanspawn can use an object of such symbolic importance to twist the very concept of Law and Justice. Whether it will influence only mortal society, or the gods as well, there is no way you can allow the enemy to hold this ritual. Oh, and while you`re at it, try not to draw any suspicious gazes. The authorities might think you`re the thief.<br /> <br /> <b>020)</b> Remember that weaver, who supposedly died as a result of Susanoo-no-Mikoto`s twisted hobby of flaying horses? Well, she is alive, simply banished to the mortal world, since no impurity can exist close to Amaterasu. But the weaver has not lost her skill, and a certain divinity really wants a furisode made by her for his daughter. Find the weaver, convince her to work... and make sure she never finds out the garment is for Susanoo`s child. Or... perhaps this is a chance for mending a broken relationship?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5530-xanthias","name":"Xanthias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-05T13:24:13-07:00","id":469574,"title":"","content":"21) It is said that when you work for your meal, it tastes much better. Your brother, popularly known as the Warrior Chef has a peculiar hobby of challenging great warriors to battle, and then eating those he slays in victory. One day, he comes before you with his famous cleaver and butcher's knife and tells you that their enemies have finally assembled an assassination squad to take him out. Are you going to stand by your brother and help him fight off a group of angry Scions, or will you join the hit squad and put this cannibal down? He's getting hungry, and those blades look pretty sharp!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T12:47:20-07:00","id":476212,"title":"","content":"<b>22)</b> You have famous guests. One of them is Narad Muni - a wonderful conversationalist, but a trickster and troublemaker as well. You might wonder whether his tongue has a mind of it`s own. The other guest is the rishi Durvasas, and... well, good luck trying to please him. Try not to get cursed.<br /> <br /> <b>23)</b> Creiddylad has had enough. Every Beltayne her two suitors, Gwyn ap Nudd and Gwythyr ap Greidawl, fight for her hand - and neither wins. What does a young goddess, embodiment of spring and youth, do? Wait until the sky falls down? No way. She wants either the Winter king or the Summer one to win - and damn the consequences. And if you dont help her (or find another solution), she will intervene herself, so you have a week to sort this mess out, or else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5530-xanthias","name":"Xanthias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T22:23:25-07:00","id":479913,"title":"","content":"Inno A Satana<br /> 24) The Church of Satan is headed by somebody a Hel of a lot more &quot;real-deal&quot; than Anton La Vey. Your mission, should you choose to accept it?<br /> Help him out by throwing the most raucous party possible.<br /> <br /> Shameless Self Promotion<br /> 25) A Scion of a Rival God is running amok as a &quot;superhero&quot; and spreading the faith far and wide. This being the 21st Century, the Scion's deeds<br /> are broadcast by every major news organization in the world and uploaded onto sites like Youtube. The Dodekatheon finds this to be a bit...hubristic.<br /> Take the Scion down a peg, if you will, but keep in mind you're messing with a real deal Internet Sensation.<br /> <br /> Bulls and Bears<br /> 26) Somebody is wreaking international havoc in the stock markets and makes Jordan Belfort and Bernie Madoff look like pikers.<br /> It is determined to be supernatural. Do you put an end to it or do you join in? Bullish or bearish?<br /> <br /> Lord of All Fevers and Plagues<br /> 27) A high-powered agent of Nergal is spreading disease and madness all throughout New Mexico.<br /> You are The Last Best Hope To Stop It. Anybody got a Birthright Hazmat suit?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5686-neckbeard","user":"Neckbeard","date":". 04-14-2015, 01:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5686-neckbeard","name":"Neckbeard","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T07:49:02-07:00","id":510651,"title":"","content":"<b>28)</b> A Man in Town who has strange Dreams , has startet to create all kinds of weird stuff (even smithing weapons), wich are all Relics. As his Dreams grow in intesity , so more powerful are the Relics he creates, its just a matter of Time until he creates something realy epic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/24.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/619-deadguy","name":"DeadGuy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T09:54:55-07:00","id":512089,"title":"","content":"<b>029)</b> you just received a call from the library, complaining that some books on divorce law are several months overdue. As it turns out, Hera gave them your contact details instead of her own. Your goal is to find and return the books without angering any of the Dodekatheon, good luck.<br /> <br /> For added trouble, she did the exact same thing with your rival.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T21:41:29-07:00","id":528516,"title":"","content":"<i>Time to add some of my specialties to the mix...</i><br /> <br /> 030) There's tryouts for a new basketball team, looking for all up-and-coming stars. It's only after you get drafted that it becomes quite clear that a different sport's being played. Turns out this is poktapok, the Maya version of the Mesoamerican ballgame, and the two coaches are the Hero Twins, Hunahpu and Xbalanque. Turns out, they're trying to assemble the perfect team to invade the underworld and take on the Lords of Xibalba once again. And once you've signed up, saying no just isn't an option... <br /> <br /> 031) You're an established Scion of some acclaim with the animal kingdom. You're known among mortals and gods alike as caring for your four-legged friends. So, you wake up one day to find a herd of glowing rainbow colored llamas on your doorstep, along with a note. It's from Urcuchillay, the Peruvian llama deity, and he's tasked you with taking care of his flock. See, they're meant to be sacrificed to the Inca pantheon as a whole on their next feast day, but something's come up, so he handed his llamas over to you. It's not entirely clear, but if these llamas are sacrificed, the recipient gets a lot of power. If you're not a Scion of the Incas, your own divine parent may want that instead (and even if you are, your parent may decide that no one ELSE truly deserves this honor, they should really have the whole herd). However, if you fail, you have an entire pantheon of angry gods with a penchant for causing natural disasters out for your blood. Not to mention the various other predators looking for some of that tasty tasty meat. And, to top it all off, these llamas apparently lack any sense of self-preservation. <br /> <br /> 032) You're a Scion of the Aztecs, and you've just been married to a Scion of another pantheon. Details about this can vary (maybe it's arranged politically, maybe it's a shotgun marriage, maybe it's a Bandmate or NPC your character's fallen in love with), but as you're about to head off on your honeymoon, you're called by Huitzilopochtli. He tells you, in no uncertain terms, that, rather than consummate this union, you must ritually sacrifice your spouse and make their skin into a garment, and then wear it in the presence of their pantheon. His commanding voice tells you that he will not accept any other outcome. What do you do?<br /> <br /> 033) The Greek gods are running short on their supply of moly, the protective herb once used to protect Odysseus from being transformed by Circe. The herb's powers are manifold, and are needed again. It's said that some might exist in the Amazon rainforest, and the rumors are true... but the only crop is in the realm of the terrifying and uncooperative Yurupari, forest god of the Brazilian Tupi Indians. He can turn the forest into an impenetrable maze of trees, and trying to find safe haven may result in you running into his crooked maw. Escaping him and stealing it is difficult, even if you could find your way through, he can be any animal in the jungle. He is a very strong fighter and resilient, not to mention a master of deadly poisons. If you wish to negotiate for the moly, there are only two ways to do so. Either you can find a woman worthy of being the wife of his father, Guaracy, the sun god (though he has impossible standards and is very misogynist even by the standards of most gods). Or... (If you're a male) you can beat him in a contest... and presents to you a mask and a flute, and tells you to start dancing. Yes, the nightmarish forest demon challenges you to the Native Amazonian equivalent to a rock off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/267-griffinguy24","name":"griffinguy24","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar267_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T05:41:05-07:00","id":528730,"title":"","content":"<b>034)</b> And they said Hercules had tough trials to worry about. You've fallen in love with another Scion and the two of you plan to get married. However, their parents don't like you very much and claim in order to prove yourself worthy, you must pass a trial, and then another, then another, then another, and eventually it becomes clear they have no intention of letting you marry your lover. So what do you do?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T10:10:52-07:00","id":528911,"title":"","content":"<b>035) </b>Oh those nutty Aztecs. Their need for blood sacrifices to fuel their power is unnerving at best. and downright disturbing at worst. And now, they have their Scions running around cutting the hearts out of every other pantheon's Scions. That'll need to stop now, before they tip the balance of power too far in their favor. I mean, it's not like anyone in your band is an Aztec Scion, right? R-right!?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6161-d38boss","name":"D38Boss","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6161_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T10:17:25-07:00","id":528914,"title":"","content":"<b>36)</b> Fun for the Greek Scions. Hera arrives, in all her godly glory, and then proceeds to break down. The goddess of marriage and its sanctity, she just can't take Zeus' philandering any more. It's affecting more than her pride and her feelings. The living embodiment of marriage's own marriage is a shambles and she's literally losing her mind. She begs the Scions for help. Zeus is Fated to be overthrown by his son. This is known. If a son of Zeus happens to be one of the Scions Hera begs him to build up his strength and take the throne. If not then she pleads with them to find a willing son of Zeus who will and help him take the throne. And Zeus' life. Unable to divorce Zeus, Hera's only hope is her husband's death.<br /> <br /> No pressure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2608-squee","name":"Squee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2608_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T10:23:26-07:00","id":528920,"title":"","content":"<b>037) </b>Damn him... Another Scion has become the favorite of all Pantheons. Somehow he has brokered a truce between the gods, brought more power to them, and even driven back the Titans! Or has he? This could all be a clever ruse by the Titans to lower the god's defenses! Is this a game of intrigue and espionage? Or is this only the calm before the storm as an all out war brews on the horizon; and you're the first and last line of defense? Only time will tell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6161-d38boss","name":"D38Boss","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6161_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T15:54:24-07:00","id":529361,"title":"","content":"038) So, you, like most people, aren't too thrilled about Aztec sacrifices. They're not happening at the same rate they did before the Spanish conquered in Mexico, but the efforts of the gods both in rural areas and in their Terra Incognitae have kept them afloat. Now, with the Titans out, their Scions are stepping up to the plate. Well, the other gods aren't having it anymore. They make it absolutely clear that the sacrifices have to stop, convincing their mortal cults and their Scions to stop cutting out people's hearts. And it works! No more people are dying on stone alters for a group of savage, backwards gods. I wonder why no one ever tried this before... <br /> <br /> ... Wait, why aren't children being born? Where'd these new diseases come from? Why isn't it raining anywhere? Why aren't crops growing at all? Where the hell did the sun go? Why are terrifying skeletal demons descending from the stars and eating people? Well... looks like we've got to get the blood flowing again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/267-griffinguy24","name":"griffinguy24","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar267_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T08:07:23-07:00","id":529960,"title":"","content":"<b>039)</b> Set , Loki , Sun Wukong and Susano-o ,went out to make Party on Earth . You there Mortal Scion ! The Gods bestow upon you the Honor to clean up their mess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/24.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/619-deadguy","name":"DeadGuy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T08:46:02-07:00","id":529999,"title":"","content":"040) Global warming...it affects us all; man, woman, tree, root, twig, frost giant...wait what?! Relax scion, they're here to talk, these Jotnar. Seems that since Odin murdered Ymir there's been no direction for the Overtitan of Frost and that's thrown things waaay out of balance. It's not like all the Jotnar were going to go work for Surtr, that'd be madness. But their leader Utgard-Loki has a plan to rectifiy the situation and restore balance to nature, he just needs you to grab a few things from some obscure places (many of which are controlled by the gods). He doesn't care how you get them, he just needs them to realize his plan, and you'll be doing a future titanrealm ruler a solid that he'd owe you forever for! He's already pointed out that there have been titans who sided with the gods (or at least stayed neutral), and this could be another one. Is this just another insidious plot by obvious titanspawn to grab power? Can these frosty bastards be trusted even if they don't have an actual titan ruler?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T08:29:26-07:00","id":531036,"title":"","content":"<b>41)</b> As a God, you now possess an own Sanctum. When Asking other Gods who build it ,they just scratch their heads , they never cared to count all those Buildings and research their History ( thats a task for servants) ,they just had a free one, standing there and ready for taking , so they gave it to you. Unbeknownst to anybody ,something starts to awake and moves through the unattended Corridors.<br /> <br /> <b>42)</b> Despite the Fact that you are a God now, you never met your true Parents , neither Mortal nor Divine. Starting to questioning your Patron , he/she just replys, that he/she didnt know either, saying that he/she just found a promising Person with divine heritage that nobody seems to has visitate yet. After some Amount of Research , you found your real Mortal Mother . You not going to leave until she told you everything you demand.<br /> <br /> <b>43)</b>Some relics ,that are supposed to play a fatefull part in History , are locked away in a Box . Its a big Secret , that only less than a Handfull of Gods know about , and they tasked you, to guard it , but the Curiosity is gnawing on you . Just a small look , what could possibly go wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/24.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/619-deadguy","user":"DeadGuy","date":". 05-29-2015, 08:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/619-deadguy","name":"DeadGuy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T14:40:06-07:00","id":532302,"title":"","content":"<b>44)</b> Fate has decreed that you and you alone can stop this new Titan Spawn who has been giving the Scions so much trouble recently. However, somebody tipped them off and now they seem to be avoiding you at every opportunity. They're always gone by the time you show up to stop their rampage, and nobody else has been able to defeat them so far. Who's leaking info about your activities to the Titan Spawn, and why?<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>45)</b> Its post Ragnarok and all the gods are dead or severely weakened by the catastrophe that swept through the Heavens. But as Fate would have it, this is not the end of the divines, but rather a new beginning. The thrones of the heavens remains empty and new tenants are required to fill them. The Scions who survived Ragnarok are now presented with a vision, for those who manage to achieve divinity shall sit upon the thrones as the creator gods of a new world. That's right, the earth is getting a reboot, and you might just have a hand in rebuilding it. There's just one problem though, there are more Scions in the world than available positions. Those wishing to become the new creator gods engage in a full on civil war, determined to eliminate the competition and increase their chance of ascending to the thrones!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 05-29-2015, 07:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T22:14:15-07:00","id":536506,"title":"","content":"46) After your last adventure your band takes it easy in a nice, normal (yet boisterous) bar. After getting a few tankards in you the stories fo your recent exploits start flowing; all the embellished details about that bastard giant you all just put down with the flying sword. As soon as you mention that detail one of the guys your band was drinking with goes immediately sober and gets this wild look in his eyes as he exclaims, &quot;:A sword that dances?! Levanteinn!!! THEY FINALLY FOUND IT! I'm GETTING THE PIG!&quot; You have this one chance to talk Freyr (for it can be none other than he) out of rampaging through town to get his lost sword back before all hell breaks loose, and try to deal with the issue more subtly. The fact that Thor, Tyr, and Balder are right there egging him on does NOT help you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T15:48:20-07:00","id":620656,"title":"","content":"I rather enjoy Story hook threads, mind if I add a few (I say even though I know you can't reply until after I've posted them.)<br /> <br /> 47) Someone claiming to be a Scion of Fenris has established a &quot;Church of Fenris&quot;, in the local area. It seems to be a fairly standard cult, with no signs of a titanic plot going on beyond the most superficial, no less.<br /> <br /> When confronted, the self-proclaimed child of Fenris claims this his father has been making increasingly desperate attempts to free himself from his chains, is trying to carve new fate for himself that leads to the freedom he so desires, it may even change his role in ragnarok.<br /> <br /> He even claims that he wishes to negotiate for Fenris's defection to the side of the gods. It carries a price though, in addition to freedom, he wants to see gleipnir destroyed, broken such that it can never be repaired.<br /> <br /> Is this all just a titanic plot? Few can deny that Fenris has the motivation. Spending nearly an eternity in chains is less than fun, after all....<br /> <br /> 48) The sun hasn't set in <i>days</i>, in fact, it's been morning across the entire world for a week, with multiple suns clearly visible, during all hours. The various gods of night, the moon, and stars, are less than pleased. Not to mention what's been going on with mortals.<br /> <br /> And you thought eternal <i>night</i> would be the problem.<br /> <br /> (This is where I apologize for the lack of quality in my ideas.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Currently Playing:</b> <i>A large, mixed splat game of <b>CofD</b>.</i> <b>As:</b> Seraph du Salomon, Voice on the concordance. Unsubtle man reluctantly participating in the business of Magi. Awakening 2E homebrew <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1338514-house-du-salomon-a-proximus-dynasty?_=1569864567692\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...=1569864567692</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2598-gryphon-s-feather","name":"Gryphon's Feather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2598_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"215"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T18:25:52-07:00","id":620772,"title":"","content":"Sunrise for a solid week? Well shit, the earth is a fiery hellscape now. And yeah, go ahead and post more ideas. We haven't had any new ones in a while. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Going to try and think of some new ones, myself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-24T19:49:17-07:00","id":638713,"title":"","content":"<b>49.)</b> Alright rookie, you who Metis is right? No? What are they teaching kids these days?...That was rhetorical, anyway, Metis is a Titan woman that Zeus had an affair with that he ate due to a prophecy that their son would overthrow his old man. Thing is, she was pregnant when she went down the storm god's gullet. She gave birth, the offspring was poking around Zeus's skull with a spear, and when the big guy got his local smith, AKA Hephaestus, to smash his skull open to figure out what was going on in there, out popped a fully grown child of Zeus and Metis. And so Athena was born. What? No I'm not done, that's just background 'cause you don't know what you should.<br /> <br /> Anyway, Metis <i>somehow</i>, I don't get paid enough to know the specifics, escaped from Zeus's belly and sought asylum with a foreign pantheon. Now Zeus figured out pretty quickly where she went, so Zeus storms up to Mexico City demanding that Huitzilotpoctli hand over Metis. Now the thing is, you at least know about a minor disagreement that the Aztec Empire had with a spaniard named Cortez right? Well it turns out that Cortez's mother was yet another of Big Z's one-night-poontangs. Oh he never got a Visitation or even Child Services, but even so the Teotl ain't too fond of Big Z. So of course they refuse to give Metis back.<br /> <br /> So Big Z starts gathering up allies, callin' in favors and the like while the Teotl do the same, and pretty soon it's the Cold War all over again, but this time it's not Uncle Sam and Mother Russia aiming nukes at each other by proxy, oh no, this time it promises to be the biggest divine war ever since the gods locked up the GTs! Oh for the love of, Greater Titans.<br /> <br /> <b>50.)</b> Okay, first off, are you from a bunker, vault, or are you some poor sap from the wilderness? Really? Huh, honestly didn't expect that. In any case, growing up did you ever hear or read any Norse Mythology? Yes I realize you didn't get a great deal of free time but I had to ask. Okay, long story short, the death of the gods and the end of the world, Ragnarok, begins with the mother of all winters: Fimbulvintr. Hold all questions until I finish. Now, at first no one thought much of when the nukes fell. The thing is, three years in, the Norns have spoken up and finally told us, we're in Fimbulvintr.<br /> <br /> <b>51.)</b> Ah good morning young sir, so good to have another child of the *sniff* Aesir visit our fine establishment. Oh do not worry, no passerby will hear our conversation. Now, what brings you to London? You were visited by a woman that told you that you are the child of a heathen god and directed you here? At least you were already in England, we have had some come to us from the far off Colonies. I am sorry to inform you that yes it is true, the heathen gods of the Viking barbarians, the Ancient Greeks and Egyptians, and who knows where else all exist. What this means for good, honest Christians like yourself is something that you will have to determine on your own.<br /> <br /> For now, you are welcome within these walls. You will be given a bed to sleep in, three meals a day, and plenty of training to keep you busy. What? I'm sorry, but now that you have received a Visitation all the monsters of myth will be hunting you. Though you look to be a strong, strapping lad I doubt you have ever had to fight for your life before.<br /> <br /> Pardon the change in subject, but just a forewarning do not stray out at night. There is a serial killer on the loose that the papers have taken to calling Jack the Ripper.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7395,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7395-meribson","user":"Meribson","date":". 08-27-2015, 10:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7395-meribson","name":"Meribson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7395_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-28T19:12:24-07:00","id":643692,"title":"","content":"<b>52)</b> When life gives you lemons, squirt juice in it's eye! All you wanted to do was live a normal life. But after receiving your visitation, that became impossible with the constant attacks Fate is throwing your way. You've tried to keep your identity a secret, you've tried attending school, even getting a part time job, but it's only been a month now and already you've been attacked 3 times on your way to work, twice while attending school, and they almost tracked you back home just yesterday. Retaining your secret identity from the public is becoming more difficult than you would like to think about. Even your friends are becoming suspicious when you spontaneously have to leave in a hurry, just before disaster strikes and a masked crusader arrives to save the day. Fortunately for you, it seems Fate has a sense of humor, and nobody has put the pieces together that you and this masked hero are one in the same. Then one day, you're approached by a group of students who claim they're in the same predicament as you. They were less than pleased to receive their own visitations and have been trying to maintain a normal life. Working together, you may be able to ease the stress of your Scion duties and keep your secret identity a while longer.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>High school super hero story.</b><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-30T12:44:16-07:00","id":645723,"title":"","content":"53) Competition was fierce in a surfing tournament off the coast of Hawaii, but you\u2019d been practicing for months to step up your skills and it was paying off. Many had remarked that you were so much more graceful and relaxed on the high seas than you were on land (on land you tended to be a klutz!). Now in the finals it was between you and some guy nobody knew about. He\u2019d been giving you the stink eye the whole tournament and now you were racing him down the waves. You were pulling ahead until he suddenly surged at you in defiance of physics to menace you with a bone-carved knife baring very inhuman fangs. He never made it; instead he was snatched below the waves by very dangerous looking tentacles and never seen again. You won the competition but didn\u2019t go near the water till the sun went down. Everyone assumed that the other surfer lost control of his board and was killed in a riptide, but you knew what actually got him. <br /> You stood at the docks thinking about this very fact when they creature returned, snatching you off the docks more quickly than you could scream and dragging you to the depths. It deposited you in a cavern beneath the waves amidst the bones of all manner of creatures, and as it reared up you could see that it was some kind of huge squid-monster. The first thing you screamed out was \u201cdon\u2019t eat me!!!\u201d which gave the creature pause as it gazed at you.<br /> \u201cWhy would I eat you my son?\u201d it replied in mild tones.<br /> It was some time before Tangaroa was finally able to get you to calm down, but since then you\u2019ve been charged with seeking out and eliminating evils from the depths.<br /> <br /> 54) The much larger whaling ship cut past you and your friends\u2019 smaller fishing trawler with obvious disdain. It had the advantage in the gathering storm whereas you and your crew were likely to be dumped into the ocean at any minute. But it was worth it, these whaling vessels would continue despoiling the sea and destroying its gentlest wildlife if they were not stopped. Your plan here was to attack them the instant they readied their weapons to fire and try to make the sinking of the ship look like an accident. You had all kinds of (very illegal) explosives on board to use on them, and a crew of similarly motivated people to help you. <br /> Your smaller craft harassed theirs for some time before the storm broke over you both. As soon as the seas began to churn your ship had its hands full just trying to keep afloat while the larger vessel chugged along unhindered. You were in the cabin when you saw it; the seas became a whirling maelstrom that sucked in both ships. You ordered the rest of your crew below hoping to save them while you tried to steer your ship out of impending doom. The larger whaling vessel didn\u2019t fare much better, its mass suddenly working against it. All of a sudden a colossal snake-like creature burst forth from the center of the maelstrom, entangling the whaling ship in its coils and crushing it. With a blood-curdling roar it set about dispatching each and every one of the whaling crew, and then it turned its shark-cold gaze upon you.<br /> You hadn\u2019t even realized you were screaming the whole time this was going on, you thought it was all your mates belowdecks. When the creature emerged all around your craft, shielding you from the storm in the process, it jarred you right out of your panic to hear it call you by name and tell you \u201cCease your screaming my child, it is embarrassing for us both!\u201d<br /> After Ryujin\u2019s stern admonishment you have continued your work on the high seas, attacking those who would defile the seas with their excesses.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-30T16:56:44-07:00","id":646097,"title":"","content":"God Level ones<br /> <br /> 55) A god of sinister reprutation but indispensable to the pantheons and the war just got murdered. The resident god of the dead confirms the god appeared in their domains without any memory of the assasination. Are there Titanspawn lurking in your Overworlds? Did someone just resolved an old grudge at a very bad moment. Do you even want to bring Loki or Sutekh or Tezcapolica back to life to continue their hinjinks?<br /> <br /> 56) You are contacted by the Nemesis who implore you to let her try to punish one of her fellows Avatars. Choice candidates are Kagusutchi for his matricide, Cronos for the castration thing, Mixcoatl of the Aztecs for the possible rape and murder of his mother (plus the quasi extinction of his brothers) or even fellow Order Titan Bress the Beautiful prince of the Fomorian and incarnation of Tyranny. While she assures her punishement will not kill them and that she will reward you for your help in bringing justice to the world (And she is not lying, the Nemesis doesn't lie), there must be a reason your parents gods didn't do a thing like that already. Will you accept or refuse with the risk of being targeted for obstruction to the rightful laws of the universe?<br /> <br /> 57) Under the influence of progressive new members the Greek Gods are engaged in peace talks with some of the Titans. While it is out of the question to make peace with Cronos, Ga\u00efa and Ouranos could perhaps be placated. The pantheon has fashioned a relic penis for the latter to be restored to full manhood and be able to take the helm of the Sky Titan. While the Avatar will accept any pact in his state and sure oaths are an important thing to Greeks even Titans, you are not too sure of the consequences of all this. Oh and if you are or know a Greek God with Health, you are charged with the negotiations. <br /> <br /> Not exactly plot hooks but long terms ambitions a Scion could take at CC<br /> <br /> ) Becoming the new Norse god(ess) of the dead letting Hel running free across the worlds and make her own Fate<br /> <br /> ) Even if sacrificing to gods others than the Teotl have no practical effects, worship is a sweet thing especially if you are not in the world risking Fatebonds, You are tasked by your parent to rebuild the old religion and bring back the old practices.That could be problematic.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2225-ganonso","name":"ganonso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-30T23:01:06-07:00","id":646370,"title":"","content":"<b>58)</b> Well that's just great, you went and got yourself a fate bond and now everybody with a hint of mystical talent is proclaiming you to be the Chosen One. Thing is, nobody knows exactly what the hell that means. Details on your destiny are vague at best, they just know you're destined to be a great hero. How or why you attain that greatness will be revealed in time, which is a fancy way of saying nobody knows! God, you hate it when prophecies are deliberately cryptic!<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>59) </b>One of your sisters has got it into her head that she's a real life Wonder Woman, which comes off as more amusing than ludicrous. Except she's decided that she wants to legitimize her role by creating the island of Thymascira, a nation populated entirely by warrior women and which men are forbidden to step foot on. She's been going around the world abducting women to become citizens of her private island while attacking any men that come close to her borders. This little joke has gone on long enough, it's time to take down this would be amazon princess!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-01T15:38:43-07:00","id":648418,"title":"","content":"60) You are the previous poster sister and know damn well he's trying to stop stop your glorious mission vision of liberating womankind from the tyranny of man's world. Kick his ass in the name of loving submission.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-01T18:52:18-07:00","id":648504,"title":"","content":"61) A local scion of Loki has given you a &quot;gift&quot;... By which I mean you, and your band, have received a cult that worships... less than flattering versions of you. While the worship <i>is</i> rather nice, you should probably correct them before you get fatebound.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Currently Playing:</b> <i>A large, mixed splat game of <b>CofD</b>.</i> <b>As:</b> Seraph du Salomon, Voice on the concordance. Unsubtle man reluctantly participating in the business of Magi. Awakening 2E homebrew <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1338514-house-du-salomon-a-proximus-dynasty?_=1569864567692\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...=1569864567692</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2598-gryphon-s-feather","name":"Gryphon's Feather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2598_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"215"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T07:52:26-07:00","id":648962,"title":"","content":"62) One of your siblings has challenged you to a 'friendly competition' to prove who's the better survivalist. All you have to do is race to the top of Mt. Everest without relying on your divine powers. What they failed to take into account was the mountain is home to a legion of Frost Giants who don't take kindly to trespassers on their mountain. If you don't make it to the top, you'll lose the challenge, but if you call on your powers, you'll forfeit!<br /> <br /> So what's more important to you, your pride or your life?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T20:22:09-07:00","id":653446,"title":"","content":"<b>63.)</b> Apparently, a Vegas snake charmer decided to up his act. With a Nemean Cobra. Now, anyone even half familiar with Nemeans could tell you that a mortal trying to charm a Nemean is a recipe for disaster. The only thing is, he's been doing it for a week and as far as anyone can tell its working. Find out if this snake charmer is, a titan cultist, a secret Scion, whatever. After all, he certainly isn't a mere mortal. Right?<br /> <br /> <b>64.)</b> You've just beaten a terrible titanspawn, and Thor has invited you to come to Asgard to drink and celebrate! Oh? The Tuatha will be there? And Dionysus and Eris too...Maybe you should take a rain check.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7395,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7395-meribson","user":"Meribson","date":". 09-05-2015, 11:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7395-meribson","name":"Meribson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7395_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T21:46:07-07:00","id":653490,"title":"","content":"<b>65)</b> You've figured out a way to stop Ragnarok from happening. It's a simple matter of binding Muspelheim so it can't bring harm to the Aesir anymore. Heck, if the dwarves can bind Fenrir for thousands of year, there's no reason why you (a scion of the forge) shouldn't be able to do the same thing! But creating restraints strong enough to bind a Greater Titan are going to require some very obscure ingredients, mortals would even deem them scientifically impossible to craft with, let alone obtain. But you have the knowledge and power of the gods, so mortal science means nothing to you!<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>66)</b> As a Trickster, you've always prided yourself on your sense of humor and ability to leave mortal and deity alike in confused bewilderment. But as with anybody who takes pride in their work, you long for a challenge. Something that will allow you to sit back and smile with a sense of accomplishment once it all comes to fruition. You're not just planning your next practical joke this time, you're going the whole way. It's your biggest joke of all time and the entire world is your target!<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T00:17:47-07:00","id":665430,"title":"","content":"67) Columbia, daughter of Athena, and former President of the Yankee Pantheon comes to you with a big smile and a nice spiel about the upcoming &quot;election&quot;. Ol Uncle Sam's been in office too long, according to her, and she's looking for funds of prayer to win her the votes necessary to overthrow him. America has been on the rocks lately (and all these titan attacks aren't helping), maybe a change of leadership would be good. On the other hand, her previous tenure as president wasn't exactly all sunshine and roses. But she's here now, and she has connections in your home country you'd never have otherwise...maybe a small contribution wouldn't be noticed by Uncle Sam<br /> <br /> 68) (Hero level) The Golem of Prague is up and moving and sees fit to punish every person in the city not following the Law of the Torah to the letter (which, if you've never read it, is just about EVERYONE). Unfortunately, Rabbi Lowe did a damn good job on his monster and the stupid thing no-sells everything in your arsenal...it is however, also very chatty. Maybe you can reason with it...or at least, talk it to death.<br /> <br /> 69) (obligatory) Aphrodite is bored (why yes, today IS one of those days. Why do you ask?) and as such bothers her favorite set of sexy young heroes with a challenge. A new sex position, find one. And while Aphrodite has a bit of a reputation as a flake, in her purview her mastery is unquestioned. (yes, she read the Kama Sutra, no, she wasn't impressed, and the newer books just repeat the older ones). Therefore your only chance is to find ANOTHER love goddess, and convince her to hand over one of the things that makes her unique to her chief rival (yes, it may ALSO be one of those WEEKS)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I'M SORRY, I CAN'T HEAR YOU OVER THE SOUND OF HOW MANY MALFEAS CHARMS I HAVE!!!</b><i>~King Crazy Genius</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/345-kandagger","name":"Kandagger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar345_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T07:07:51-07:00","id":665665,"title":"","content":"70) (Demi God) One of your rivals has garnered quite the reputation. Since the time of their visitation, they have successfully hunted every species under the sun, moon and sea. Their trophy room has every beast to ever stalk the earth stuffed and mounted somewhere on the wall, floor or ceiling. There's only one thing they have yet to hunt, the most dangerous game of all. No, not man, they killed one of those last month. This month, they're hunting for Scion, and having been rivals for so long, they consider you to be a worthy hunt!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T17:16:49-07:00","id":674690,"title":"","content":"71) Zeus, regarded as one of the most powerful gods in the entire war. A being so mighty, he thinks he can get away with anything and damn the consequences. Unfortunately for him, it's time somebody beat some humility into him. Fate has decreed that one of Zeus' own sons would bring him down some day and now it seems that ancient prophecy is stirring awake. You are a Scion of Zeus, and your relationship with the old man is less than happy. Raping your mother and abandoning her to an early grave raising you probably didn't give Zeus a ringing endorsement either. No, you've been holding a grudge for a while now and it's time to exact your revenge! But you're no fool, Zeus is said to have more power than the entire pantheon combined, which means you're going to need allies, lots of allies. Hell, you might just need <i>an army!</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T02:34:44-07:00","id":695900,"title":"","content":"72) Whelp, someone just went and shattered the mystical agreement between pantheons to cease overt meddling in mortal affairs. Of course, no god particularly wants to risk getting fatebound, especially considering the rather twisted portrayals of many of them in modern fiction. <br /> <br /> But there are a few gods who won't let that stop them. Coyote, for one, has some long over-due issues to take up with the American government regarding the treatment of his people, and once the other gods notice its only a matter of time before other gods descend to settle their own thousand-year-old grudges, with mortals caught in the middle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1457-quanutmshard","name":"Quanutmshard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T06:59:09-07:00","id":696031,"title":"","content":"<b>73)</b> The Rapture has begun. A demigod who specializes in the Guardian purview has begun to personally escort mortals to the Overworld in hopes of keeping them protected from the encroaching Titan Spawn terrorizing the world. The mortals call them the 'chosen people' but the gods call them <i>refugees.</i> The Overworld is already crowded enough without throngs of scared, confused mortals lining up at the gates clamoring to get in. You and your band have been sent to resolve this issue before it turns into a full blown riot.<br /> <br /> It doesn't seem that hard. You just need to figure out how to tell a horde of people they won't be getting into heaven and that their savior's actions are not endorsed by the rest of the pantheon. Yeah, there's no way this could go horribly wrong for either side...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-12T23:51:38-07:00","id":699533,"title":"","content":"Well, here we go then. A few of my story hooks which I actually used. <br /> <br /> <b>74) </b>You are a Scion of the Aztecs who got a creature as a gift from your godparent. Sadly, your loyal companion died in your service and your godparent is rightly furious about this. So furious in fact that he demands you bring the creature back. Quiet literally from hell, as you'll descend into the legendary depths of Xibalba, the place of fear, to face its gruesome tests and bring your companion back from the dead. <br /> <br /> <b>75) </b>As if the Amatsukami didn't have their hands full already, The Drowned Road starts making moves against them for no apparent reason. Sending Umibozu, Bake-Kujira and other horrors who possess both the Miasmic and the Piscean template, this attack is a horrible iteration of the thought what would happen when the Titans join forces. It's up to you to find out whether this was just a one-time thing between the fickle Titans, part of a much larger plot or something else entirely. And you will, of course, have to battle against the many strange and horrid things Japanese mythology has to offer when it comes to the vast depths of the sea...<br /> <br /> <b>76)</b> Maybe you crossed the wrong god. Or a Titanspawn that is very adept in Magic. Or, probably, Fate decided to have a laugh on you. Either way you find yourself in the body of another Scion from your band and the rest of them have it no better. Aside of what happens when suddenly the brawny Scion of Ares suddenly has a frail body with a brilliant mind or the booky scholar of Thoth suddenly can punch holes through steel (for some reason, no attributes are swapped...), you have to deal with the fact that this could happen again or probably be a permanent thing. And you've grown to be quiet fond of your bodies. Also, if your bodies and minds are swapped, how can the lovers of your group express their love for each other properly? Hey, get your hands of my body! Don't kiss ME, either! <br /> <br /> <b>77) </b>Kalfu is one of the more nasty gods to cross. And this time you've really done it. When one of the members of your Gang decided not to follow an order issued by him, he turns the tables on you in the most nasty way. The Scion of Bastet gets attacked by all cats she sees, the handsome Son of Amaterasu suddenly has an erectile dysfunction and every drop of alcohol that touches the lips of your Dagda-Scion suddenly turns into water. Luckily, you got a list of things you have to do and every point on this list breaks one of Kalfus curses - but in which order you don't know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8325-asmael","name":"Asmael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8325_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-14T08:34:50-07:00","id":700878,"title":"","content":"In RE 74, Why is the critter you got from your Aztec parent going to the Mayan Underworld instead of the Aztec one? Or is that part of the reason the parent is furious? The critter belongs in Mictlan, so you have to pull a Hero Twins THEN go put it where it's supposed to be?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-14T10:24:27-07:00","id":701055,"title":"","content":"As you said, basically. Also I found Xibalba to be far more interesting than Mictlan. It might be hard to persuade Mictlantecuhtli to help you, but hes still an Aztec and thus bound to at least listen to a Scion from another Aztec god. Especially if that Scion happens to be a favorite daughter of Huizilopochtli, which was the case. So I just found it to be more intriguing to re-visit the Hero Twins ordeals rather than face Ol' Skelly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8325-asmael","name":"Asmael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8325_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-14T14:59:14-07:00","id":701325,"title":"","content":"<b>78)</b> You've always wanted a puppy, but your mortal foster father was allergic to them, so he told you 'no' every time. Luckily for you, Hades is more compassionate to his children and on the day of your visitation he gives you the gift you've always wanted. A brand new <b>four headed</b> puppy! He says if you raise it properly, it could become a great servant like Cerberus and Orthros. But is that what you want; another guard dog for the gates of the underworld, or will this beast grow up to become your new best friend?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 10-25-2017, 07:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-19T16:17:08-07:00","id":709499,"title":"","content":"<b>79)</b> Cool guys don't look at explosions, they create them! There is a Scion who has ambitions on becoming a god of war some day, but believes such things as swordplay and honorable accord are the byproducts of ancient civilization and no longer relevant in today's society. In the modern world, warfare is all about destruction on a massive scale. The deadlier the weapon, the more valuable it becomes. Their approach to the Titan war favors the Scorched Earth strategy, which does seem to eliminate the targets, but causes substantial damage to the environment in the process. The gods are getting nervous, if this scion manages to ascend to divinity, their destructive tactics could lead to widespread damage of the Overworld. Destroying the heavens just to keep them out of the Titan's hands is not an option many would agree with and so they send you to negotiate a more humane approach to combat. If they prove uncooperative to such a bargain, you have authority to respond appropriately to this god blooded terrorist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 06-02-2016, 12:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T18:44:51-07:00","id":727745,"title":"","content":"<b>80)</b> Bad news, Loki has a new grandson. Worse news, his father is Fenrir who you're pretty sure was still tied up last time anybody checked. The Scion has proven to be every bit as strong as you might expect from such a heritage, which would normally make them a worthy ally in the fight against the Titans. Except that like the rest of the Aesir, they desire a way to avoid the trappings of Fate. In this particular case, they plan to assassinate Vidar and thus prevent the death of Fenrir in the time of Ragnarok!<br /> <br /> Is this Scion acting alone, or do they have allies to facilitate their plan? But more importantly, how did Fenrir conceive a Scion without anybody noticing and does Loki have some hand in this? Somebody had to give them their visitation and the list of suspects is quite small!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 06-02-2016, 12:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T05:33:16-08:00","id":751196,"title":"","content":"<b>81)</b> A village in Egypt is populated entirely by cats. Not cat people, but actual cats. The funny thing is (well, hilarious, really) that they're attempting to do people things. Working jobs, wearing garments, carrying miniature assault rifles... Obviously this village is some manner of divine prank. But did these felines used to be people, or are they simply blessed with hyper evolved intelligence? Unless you know how to speak cat, you're left with solving this mystery yourself. But once you do, how are you going to fix the issue of a feline Taliban forming within its walls?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 06-02-2016, 12:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T20:56:46-08:00","id":752953,"title":"","content":"82) Now ya done it... So after a bout of epic drunkenness you decided to chase down a rainbow to see of you could get that pot of gold people talk about (or at least some free skittles). Good news is you managed to catch one, bad news is you managed to trip up Eris the original Theoi messenger goddess while she was on the way to deliver something. Now you get to deliver this package for her, double quick, or you'll be shown a whole new <b>spectrum</b> of pain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T21:09:04-08:00","id":757901,"title":"","content":"<b>83)</b> Eccentric, it's how the upper class refer to one of their own who suffers from mental instability. So when the chief of your respective pantheon calls you up and says your 'eccentric' cousin is off their meds, it can't be a good time for anybody involved. Over the last several days, there have been reports of raining frogs, bloody fountains, an epidemic of lice and wild animals wandering into town attacking people. Every day your cousin appears before the mayor and orders him to release his slaves, which the mayor publicly denies having any idea what he's talking about. The story is popular enough that you can tell how this is going to play out if left unchecked. You decide to intervene, but is your cousin really just in need of help, or is there more going on in the boardroom than the mayor reveals?<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>84)</b> Pranking a prankster is always fun. But somebody has decided to steal all of Sun Wukong's private banana stash, leaving a sign explaining they've been requisitioned by &quot;King K Rool.&quot; Needless to say, the monkey king is not pleased at somebody stealing from his personal belongings, and has asked for your help in tracking down the culprit. The first step is figuring out why the Sun Wukong's realm is seeing an influx of crocodiles instead of primates.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>85)</b> A recently slain Scion of Hades was improperly buried without coin to pay for Charon's passage. Rather than be stranded on the other side of the River Styx for eternity, they turned around and walked back to the world of the living, bringing a host of lingering spirits with them. Now, the city is overrun with ghosts and specters looking to celebrate their come back, or having difficulty adjusting to the modern era. The city is in chaos and the mortals are terrified out of their minds. The Dodekatheon needs a band of Heroes to bust these ghosts and send the Scion back to the underworld once and for all!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 10-25-2017, 07:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-15T14:35:06-08:00","id":766544,"title":"","content":"86) Theres a new Video Game coming out and its really cutting edge! &quot;The Apotheosis&quot; goes off the shelves like the proverbial bread with its incredibly life-like graphics, immersive storytelling and unique characters. It's just.. good. Too good in fact. Apparently, a Cyclops turned Game Designer decided to hide a bit of universal truth inside the game, not so blatantly that everyone can read it but still in a way that these informations about godly endeavours might get into the wrong hands. So its for the Scions to get into the code and find all the secrets that are hidden there... Oh, and its the first VR-Game with pain-based feedback. Did we forget to tell you that? Whoops.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8325-asmael","name":"Asmael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8325_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T15:48:54-08:00","id":767391,"title":"","content":"<b>87)</b> If you want to become truly legendary, start by proving you're the greatest among your peers. A Scion has declared a world wide tournament to prove who is the greatest fighter on the planet. The tournament is reserved for battle oriented Heroes and the rules appear simple enough. The fight continues until one opponent surrenders or is unable to continue the fight. The prize for winning each match is a noticeable increase to one's popularity, which is always good to have. But the grand prize for winning the whole tournament is elevation to the rank of Demigod!<br /> <br /> Warrior Scions all over the world have registered to compete, eager to rise through the ranks in the only way they feel comfortable, by beating the crap out of their rivals!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T21:34:45-08:00","id":772797,"title":"","content":"<b>88)</b> The Megaladon, a shark of such epic proportions that it fed on blue whales as its primary food source. Mortals believe it has been extinct for millions of years. Maybe it was before the Titans broke free, but now somebody's brought one back to life. A Typhonian Shark with the jaw strength to rip through the hull of a battleship has emerged and the various sea gods are not pleased with its arrival. The environmental damage the shark wreaks upon the world's oceans from sinking oil tankers, excessive feeding habits and targeting the world's navy vessels has prompted beings like Susano-o, Poseidon, and Sobek to gather their Scions and send them on a fishing trip to bring the creature to justice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 11-14-2016, 12:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T08:45:16-08:00","id":773160,"title":"","content":"89) The seas are alive...with the sounds of MADNESS! Surviving fishermen, deep-sea oil-prospectors, and even the crewmen from smaller naval vessels who manage to survive these mysterious attacks are invariably found as gibbering masses of PTSD, all of whom blither out nonsensical tales of hideous tentacled monsters from the deeps following horrible mutant fish-people into battle against them. Tangaroa has repeatedly stated this is NOT his doing, and Ryujin got out of the tentacle business ever since hentai was developed and it got weird. You you scions get to be employed as exterminators (bait?) to catch this monstrous force in the act and end it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T18:39:10-08:00","id":781996,"title":"","content":"<b>90)</b> It takes a special kind of crazy to fund an expedition to the center of the earth. Unless that expedition is being organized by Fire Giants, then it's perfectly reasonable. Unfortunately, the giants plan to destabilize the planet's core, resulting in volcanic eruptions across the globe. The Scions are tasked with destroying the massive sized drills, collapsing the tunnels and eliminating the giants responsible before they can fuck the world beyond repair.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T00:23:26-08:00","id":782130,"title":"","content":"<b>91</b>) Your pantheon's death god(s) have you on the trail of a vampire of singular foulness, one who seeks to raise an army of the shambling dead to serve in subjugating the world of the living. Already he's made progress by absconding with the warrior dead from national cemeteries, the tabloids and papers are aflame with the scandal its caused. Survivalist nutjobs are screaming and flailing in panic at the onset of &quot;World-war Z&quot;, stores are being emptied, bunkers are filling with terrified people, it's only a matter of time before the riots and pillaging start, and with that will come the fall of civilization.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-25T23:23:38-08:00","id":792969,"title":"","content":"<b>92)</b> One of Loki's Scions is getting tired of waiting for Fimbulwinter and has decided to take a more proactive method to starting Ragnarok. He's going to start his own long winter; a nuclear winter to be precise! Your Band has to stop this crazed Scion's plans to acquire the world's missile activation codes before he unleashes not one, but two different kinds of apocalypse upon the whole world!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T16:15:22-08:00","id":797065,"title":"","content":"93) You are a Scion of Hephaestus, a brilliant Hacker who has penetrated the deepest secrets of the Dark Net. This is where you find &quot;Aztec Affictionado&quot;, a site that specializes in streaming brutal Aztec rituals with unwilling participants. This, of course, needs to stop, but which deity, if any, you'll offend by this, you don't know...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8325-asmael","name":"Asmael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8325_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T07:00:12-08:00","id":800560,"title":"","content":"94) Catching Up with Bigfoot? Ghost Hunters? These guys have nothing on Scions. A &quot;helpful&quot; fatebound mortal &quot;helps&quot; the band by finding a real Nemean Beast. (I used a Hogzilla!) Then the band is taped fighting it. Then the plan is to sell it to a major network as a monster of the week Reality TV series! What could go wrong?!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10649-silverblaze","name":"Silverblaze","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T03:29:36-08:00","id":804318,"title":"","content":"<b>95)</b> The Gods have always known that somebody freed the Titans from their prison, but were never able to figure out who. Now they know the answer to that great mystery. Fate itself kicked in the door and broke the Titan's shackles. Fate never intended for the Gods to rule eternally from their thrones in the heavens and now that they are considered obsolete in the modern world, it is time for a new generation to take over. Just as the Titans rebelled against their creators and the Gods against the Titans, so too are the Scions destined to rebel against the Gods. A new age is dawning and the Gods are now faced with an assault on two fronts!<br /> <br /> <b>Story:</b> By Fate's decree, the Scions are to replace the Gods as the overseers of a new age of human civilization. While the Gods are preoccupied diverting forces to the war effort, the Scions launch a coup against their pantheon, attempting to seize the Overworld thrones for themselves. The story is probably best played with a Band who are all from the same pantheon to make things easier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 01-09-2016, 06:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T09:47:54-08:00","id":806173,"title":"","content":"<br /> 96) When humans die and are given the proper funerary rites their souls are carried to the appropriate afterlife to be judged, sorted, and ultimately kept in trust. A displaced soul results when the proper rites (regardless of culture) are not performed and it will either linger forever as a sad ghost, or become corrupted by titanic influence and rage becoming a specter. Since the old gods fell out of favor and were replaced by modular humanistic religions, no valid examples of such rites have been performed, so where are all the dead going? The world is not awash in ghosts and specters, but the underworlds of various pantheons haven\u2019t seen much in the way of new arrivals. You\u2019ve been tasked to track down where the flood of modern souls is going, and report back to your pantheon\u2019s resident psychopomp.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T10:27:38-08:00","id":811198,"title":"","content":"97) It's been over 2,000 years but still some things never change or only a little bit: When the local Footballteam of Sparta (insert State here) is beaten by the the Troyans (enter state here) on their own Gridiron tensions are allready at a new alltime high. But only when, after the visitors have departed and are well out of town, a well liked person who was last seen chating with some Troyans is reported missing things realy start to spiral out of controll. Calling in allies and favors takes some time but soon it realy looks like the two citys are going to war ...... again. Just passing through the area the band of Scions is dregged into all of this and may find themself conscripted into service for one or maybe even both sides.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11025-ganruy","name":"Ganruy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T06:15:51-08:00","id":813320,"title":"","content":"Can I simply say that this thread is what got my interest in Scion now? *sigh* not enough hours in the day/week/month/year...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1897-ffanxii4ever","name":"ffanxii4ever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T14:36:26-08:00","id":813661,"title":"","content":"<b>98)</b> The old Gods abandoned the World because they wanted to escape the possibility of mortals transforming them beyond recognition. Yet their plan may have just backfired tremendously. Without the presence of the Gods to set the story straight, their legends began to get twisted with the retelling through the ages. The modern age presents the worst of the lot, depicting Hades to be the Greek devil, Zeus is some wise and dignified ruler, while Hera is his evil queen. Loki is mistaken to be Thor's brother and the child of a Frost Giant, while Thor is depicted as being some blond haired, blue eyed heart throb. These are just some of the more popular examples!<br /> <br /> The Gods stopped spreading their Legend, and so the mortals continued to do it for them, putting their own spin on things. If the Gods don't figure out a way to resolve this issue, they may end up falling victim to the very threat they sought to avoid. But how do they fix this mess without revealing themselves to the entire world and setting off a wide scale pandemonium?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 06-02-2016, 12:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T03:55:32-08:00","id":814761,"title":"","content":"99) Death Gods HATE him! A normal, unassuming mortal suddenly isn't all that normal and mortal at all. When he gets hit and should be killed by a car, he stands up minutes later, literally unharmed. And it doesn't stop there. After a few more accidents, meant to correct this small mistake, it becomes apparent that he is truly and utterly immortal. And the gods of the dead cannot have that. It would put them out of their jobs. So they send a few Heroes after him to find out just what exactly made him immortal - and how to correct it. After all, immortality is something only gods can truly handle. Or is it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8325-asmael","name":"Asmael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8325_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T11:17:24-08:00","id":817007,"title":"","content":"100) The world is full if disenfranchised youth, many of whom have no parental guidance, and are thrown under the bus by the system. Understandably there\u2019s a lot of rage and frustration built up there that seeks expression, but no one to give that expression form\u2026till now. Whether they were sought out by their new masters, or the rancor of the downtrodden managed to reach out on its own, there have been responses. Youth of the world are suddenly being infused with divine power and instilled with the will to vent it upon the world in general, and the gods in particular. Now bands of scions must rush to counter the threat of vengeance-crazed people infused with the powers of the titans before they destroy the world in their rage.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T13:39:21-08:00","id":817909,"title":"","content":"101) The party are all half-siblings of the same mortal father. Their Visitation was a bit unusual: it didn't involve any of their mothers. Zeus himself showed up, not to claim them, but to try to decide if he would crack up or crack skulls over this mortal man who'd fathered children on nearly every goddess in the Dodekatheon. He figures the best way to decide is to have the kids do a few tasks for him. But his wife thinks up SO much better labors, so their first task is to convince her to help a bunch of products of extramarital affairs by giving them heroic deeds by which to prove themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T14:47:03-08:00","id":817976,"title":"","content":"<b>Sorry, couldn't resist <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> 102)</b> It was just supposed to be a trick, a loop hole that allowed Pan to disobey Zeus and continue interacting with the mortal world. He wasn't really supposed to be <i>the Devil</i>. But 2,000+ years of mortal belief can change a God and now Pan's latest Scion threatens to fulfill an ancient prophecy that will plunge the World into 1,000 years of darkness! The Anti-Christ has appeared on Earth and it's up to your Band to stop his rise to power before he an his demon army conquer the World!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 02-01-2016, 06:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T08:35:17-08:00","id":821011,"title":"","content":"103) As a Scion with Years of Experience , you started to work for the Gods as a Trainer of young Scions. At the final Battle between Gods and Titans you see one of your most promising Students again,....on the side of the Titans , grinning in your Face.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/24.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/619-deadguy","name":"DeadGuy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T16:15:03-08:00","id":821282,"title":"","content":"<b>104)</b> The Dwarves dug too deep. Yeah, yeah, you've heard this story before, but back then it was only in movies and books. Now there's an actual Stygian demon prowling around under the city and <i>It. Is. Pissed!</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 02-09-2016, 04:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T11:38:03-08:00","id":825024,"title":"","content":"<br /> <b>105)</b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:22px\"> The kitsune are getting out of hand. Things are so bad, that Amaterasu Omikami herself decided to rid the world of this pest. And, of course, your band is ordered to carry out the sentence. Who else? Now, get to work. Unless, of course, your heart is not made of stone, and you ally with Inari who plans to trick the Sun Goddess herself. The unruly foxes might survive cloaked in their illusions, but you will have a hell of a time trying to get out of this unscathed.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>106)</b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:22px\"> Remember the previous time Mother Earth (no, not the titan avatar... It's complicated) complained about humanity? There was a war worthy of epics. And now... Well, She is beyond pissed. Our species has been a mistake. And there is no way you can convince Her otherwise. Have fun preparing for Kurukshetra 2.0. Now that literally everybody has a cute little nuke or ten, can the damage even be contained anymore?</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>107)</b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:22px\"> There is this immensely talented mortal musician (well, a drop of fairy blood might be responsible for his inhuman charm...). The sidhe are determined to have him come hell or high water. No way are they letting such a genius grow old and die! As it happens, you are under a geas to convince said musician to follow the white rab... sorry, stag. Hey, this eccentric guy might feel right at home among the fair folk! Hopefully, he's not planning on becoming their undisputed ruler...</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5530-xanthias","name":"Xanthias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T14:54:20-08:00","id":825106,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:26px\">You missed 104!</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T12:54:15-08:00","id":827011,"title":"","content":"But isn't yours number 104? DeadGuy posted hook 103, right? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5530-xanthias","name":"Xanthias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T13:34:22-08:00","id":827051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xanthias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/431083-101-scion-story-hooks?p=827011#post827011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But isn't yours number 104? DeadGuy posted hook 103, right?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">... damn it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> ---------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <b>108)</b> The Legend of Zeus claims that his power over lightning was a gift from the Cyclopes after the events of the first titan war. It has served Zeus well for many ages, but now they've pulled rank. The Cyclopes have gone on strike, refusing to make more lightning bolts until they are presented with better living conditions, privileges and social rights. If their demands are met, the Cyclopes could prove as valuable an ally to the Dodekatheon as the Dwarves are to the Aesir. But Zeus, being Zeus, does not appreciate being blackmailed. He demands production of his lightning bolts be resumed and is in no mood to compromise. But with limited stores of ammunition, he is forced to temper his rage for the time being.<br /> <br /> The hero's band has been assigned to resolve the issue of dealing with the Cyclopes. But which side will they choose in this conflict? Will they side with Zeus and earn the favor of the Gods, or will they side with the Cyclopes in hopes of forging an alliance with the giant craftsmen?</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 02-09-2016, 04:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-21T19:48:11-07:00","id":895840,"title":"","content":"So I'm completely new to Scion, but would &quot;the Aesir get tired of neo-Nazis appropriating their imagery and sullying their public image, so they task some mortals to kick their butts publicly&quot; be an acceptable story seed?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 05-22-2016, 02:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-21T23:34:55-07:00","id":895947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/431083-101-scion-story-hooks?p=895840#post895840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I'm completely new to Scion, but would &quot;the Aesir get tired of neo-Nazis appropriating their imagery and sullying their oublic image, so they task some mortals to kick their butts publicly&quot; be an acceptable story seed?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Interesting you should say that. In Scion Companion there is a story arc set in World War 2. Loki comes up with a grand plan for manipulating Fate Bonds so the Gods can become more powerful against the Titans. He convinces Odin to swear the Aesir's service to Loki while he encourages Hitler to start his regime. Unfortunately, Loki did not count on Hitler being a total monster. Yeah, I know, the god who wants to watch the heavens burn thinks Hitler himself went too far. It doesn't really add up, but that's how the book describes it..<br /> <br /> Anyways, the grand plan doesn't go as Loki had hoped, but the Aesir are powerless to act against Loki as long as they are bound by the oath made to him. By the end of the war, Loki frees them of their oath, allowing the Aesir to clean up their mess.<br /> <br /> <br /> Basically, after the events of WW2, the Norse pantheon cracks down HARD on the Nazi's for everything they did, despite the fact that the entire Nazi regime was started because of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 05-22-2016, 02:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-21T23:54:09-07:00","id":895953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/431083-101-scion-story-hooks?p=895840#post895840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I'm completely new to Scion, but would &quot;the Aesir get tired of neo-Nazis appropriating their imagery and sullying their oublic image, so they task some mortals to kick their butts publicly&quot; be an acceptable story seed?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ignoring the WWII section of Companion, that sounds totally reasonable. The Aesir (+3 captive Vanir in Asgard) tend to intervene personally, but if there is a reason they can't show up themselves (such as the Core explanation of 'Fate problems') I could totally see intermediaries. I don't know if the entire Pantheon would get involved (they might not all notice, or 'get' it unless they have been paying attention to world events in the 21st century) but some figures, totally. <br /> <br /> Odin, Heimdall, and Frigg (has access to Odin's throne and tends to know what he knows despite his desires) probably have noticed it, even in a setting where the Pantheons are highly withdrawn. Odin is a bit... of an odd duck, but if it bothered him (if it was doing odd things to the Pantheon's Fates, or if it was making him personally look bad), I could totally see him either showing up Avatared down as a Wanderer and running circles around a group very publicly somehow. He might use proxies for it, especially if there is a reason in the setting that the Divine can't fiddle with the world. Heimdall and Frigg both I can see getting mortals, Legendary Mortals, or Scions to intervene in some way.<br /> <br /> Though both Tyr and Thor probably wouldn't notice<i>, </i>not really being renowned for watching Midgard, but if they did they both would be very interesting. I can see Tyr using Scions or mortals to do something about it. Thor, well, Thor would probably show up himself if it offended him enough and start a fight. I don't know much about Neo-Nazi ideology, but if the anti-Slav aspects of the Nazis is still present, you could even do something very neat with Thor in that regard. We have a Russian myth eluding to Thor helping an invading force of Norse attack the native Slavs of a region (the Bogovi [Slavic Pantheon] have a non-interventionist policy and had to restrain their own Storm God, Perun, from going down and fighting back) so he actually has rare cross-cultural experience and might take the anti-Slav narratives badly after having first hand experience with them. Especially if at some point he and Perun made up.<br /> <br /> Depending on how you are representing Loki, he could either not really care (the dick borderline evil Loki he is widely represented as), or be very offended (if he is still the prankster + loyal problem solver and causer of the Pantheon) that his adopted family is being insulted. If you're using this second Loki, I could totally see him getting Scions or Mortals together to deal with a predominant group of Neo-Nazis. While he might not opt for beating them up, he might set his helpers out to destroy the organization through divine mockery and cunning. Potentially, the more long-term solution of all of the options.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T16:35:00-07:00","id":896381,"title":"","content":"If no one minds a quasi-crossover...<br /> <br /> 109: A group of mortals approaches a regional scion of Athena claiming that they are cultists of her mother, and they need her help. They're being hassled by a group of so-called &quot;hunters&quot; claiming they're a dangerous cult. They've even seen these mortals attacking lesser titanspawn creatures. So how are there two groups of mortals who not only know about the Titan war, <i>and</i> what kind of mortals can fight titanspawn and live?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T22:08:14-07:00","id":898630,"title":"","content":"<b>110. </b>Someone is selling street-corner Jotunblut to mortals in Hungary. At first it works like a megasteroid, turning its drinkers into sculpted paragons without any exercise. But prolonged use breeds aggression, and every act of aggression turns the user uglier and more brutish. Soon, these &quot;Ugri,&quot; (an old term for Hungarian which sounds strangely like &quot;Ogre&quot;) are rampaging across cities and towns, forming into warbands and doing all manner of harm. Who is distributing this tainted giant's blood, and what do they want?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11816-foxcalibur","name":"Foxcalibur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11816_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T09:26:00-07:00","id":905704,"title":"","content":"<b>111)</b> There's a band of scions (possibly the players?) who have their sights set on creating their own pantheon and stepping out of the shadow of their divine parents. Okay, there's nothing too unusual about that, lots of scions feel that way. Except that the band is comprised of children from the chiefs of all the other pantheons! The scions of the highest ranking deities in existence have all come together with the intention of creating a new religion under their rule. Can these scions be trusted to remain civilized towards the other pantheons, or is this the beginning of a sinister titan plot?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 06-02-2016, 12:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T07:20:33-07:00","id":906398,"title":"","content":"<b>Demigod to Apotheosis Hook<br /> <br /> <br /> 112)</b> You've heard of a legendary blacksmith who creates weapons for battle hardened Scions that greatly improve their abilities to fight off the Titan forces. The catch is that in addition to the monetary payment, the customers are Fate Bound to their weapon upon receiving it. Well, you found the smith and commissioned from him a mighty blade, custom designed for your specifications. You paid for the services and received the weapon as was expected. But now you found out something quite disturbing about the smith's previous customers. Shortly after receiving their weapons, they began to follow the path of violence and destruction. The smith isn't just any craftsman, <i>he is a demon</i>, and those who buy from him become commanding officers in hell's legion!<br /> <br /> You can already feel the evil radiating from your weapon, it pulls at you with urges best not spoken of out loud. Can you find a way to free yourself of the Fate you paid for, or will you give into temptation and become a demon general?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 06-03-2016, 10:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-02T07:51:12-07:00","id":924882,"title":"","content":"<b>113)</b> Sometimes the Gods choose mortal men and women to act as their prophet in the World. Often at times, these prophets are executed for heresy against some other faith, or laughed off as being crazy and false heralds. In this particular case, you really, really wish the latter had been true. Lovecraft was not merely a science fiction writer, he was a living prophet, recording the legends of the incomprehensible pantheon that features such entities as Cthulhu, Azothoth, Hastur and Shub-Niggurath. Mortals even began to erect cults dedicated to the beings depicted in his work. Now, after countless eons, the old ones have finally noticed our little mud ball is getting quite a bit of attention from other deities, and they want to find out why.<br /> <br /> The Old Ones have awoken, and now the Scions have bigger problems than Titans to worry about!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T04:43:02-07:00","id":926359,"title":"","content":"<b>114)</b> Astronomers predicted it decades ago, and now it seems the time is finally upon us. A meteor the size of our planet, if not bigger, is on a collision course for earth, and it seems that one of the Greater Titans is the one piloting it towards its destination. The movies were wrong, mankind doesn't have a weapon powerful enough to safely destroy a threat of this size before it makes impact. But perhaps the Gods can provide mortals with the technology they need to save the world?<br /> <br /> But even if they do have something that powerful in their arsenal, we still need a team of brave men and women willing to risk their lives by installing it on the meteor!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T10:35:28-07:00","id":926497,"title":"","content":"115) &quot;I got an idea...&quot; the phrase usually precludes things that are either very good or very bad. This time results are...mixed. let's not dwell on the unusually grueling battle between the guardian deities of the solar barque for now, it's not relevant just how taxing it was or how close they came to losing Ra's light. And we don't have to think about which of them, in a drunken rage, thought up the idea of taking the fight to Apep/Apophis directly and trying for a more final solution, nor should we dwell on who it was that actually devised an interesting new solution to the problem.<br /> No, what has to be addressed is the result of the &quot;brainstorming session which led to the current predicament of Apep's dark and destructive power being sealed into a human vessel. There's no way the solution is permanent, the mortal can;t just live continually right? But even though the unknowing candidate was chosen specifically for being an innocent soul with a kind nature, the fundamental aspect of the power sealed within him continually manifests as great misfortune all around him. If the candidate is killed, it will free all of Apep's power into the world directly, flooding everything with darkness and death, and transforming the normal waking world into something like unto a permanent Silent Hill. If the candidate is hurt, the power automatically retaliates to incredibly destructive ends. The seal that holds this ploy together won;t dissolve till the end of the candidate's life, which we aren't even sure is finite any longer, and we're concerned that any attempt to live out a normal life (by say siring children) may multiply the problem in horrible and unexpected ways.<br /> <br /> It goes without saying that this situation needs to be kept under wraps, but there needs to be a solution. Fast!.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T04:33:06-07:00","id":929657,"title":"","content":"<b>116)</b> What happens when you mix lycanthropy with the T-Virus? Well, at least one Scion of Loki plans to find out. They're attempting to bio-engineer an airborne variation of the Therianthrope infection, transforming the entire world's population into man-beasts as part of an agreement with Terra. You don't know where their primary lab is located yet, but you do know they're not working on this project alone. They have their own band who supports them, which means this won't be as easy as just kicking down the door and torching the specimens!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>117)</b> A cult of Terra has been abducting Scions early in their Legends and forcing them to participate in gladiator matches for the entertainment of blood thirsty Titan Spawn. Sometimes the matches are singular duels, and other times they're a team effort. Regardless of how the matches are set up, the Scions are promised freedom if they can achieve 100 consecutive victories. Unfortunately, nobody has been able to defeat the arena's grand champion so far, and now you're one of the captives!<br /> <br /> The rules of the arena are as follows<br /> <br /> 1 - Matches are set up according to estimated skill of the combatants involved.<br /> <br /> 2 - Fights are to the death.<br /> <br /> 3 - Disqualified combatants are fed to Nemean Lions.<br /> <br /> 4 - Members of the same team can not be pitted against each other.<br /> <br /> 5 - Slaves must achieve 100 <i>consecutive</i> victories to earn their freedom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 07-11-2016, 07:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T08:40:55-07:00","id":930872,"title":"","content":"<b>118)</b> It's all over the news: Suicide bombings on American soil! So far, all of the targets have been Moonbeans Coffee Shops, but no one knows why. No organization has taken credit for the bombings. Weirdest of all, there are some rumors that it's not intentional bombings at all, that somehow the coffee itself is causing people to spontaneously and destructively combust. Meanwhile, word comes down from &quot;on high&quot; that the powerful, mad ghost of Kaldi the Shepherd (the legendary inventor of coffee) has escaped from the control of the Pesedjet and stolen away a powerful Relic. Could the two be related? (Hint: You bet they could!)<br /> <br /> <b>119)</b> An oil derrick in the Gulf of Mexico was abandoned after their drills found not the rich oil deposit they expected, but some kind of massive undersea cave. Now the sea underneath the derrick is a perpetual whirlpool, drawing things down and never letting them up again. In reality, the greedy drillers have broken a small hole into the Drowned Road, specifically the depths where Cipactli swims. If only the hole were bigger (much, much bigger) the Titan could break through and swim the Earth's waters again.<br /> <br /> To make matters worse, a group of American spring-breakers have discovered the whirlpool, and the strange creatures that swim out of it. They've come to the conclusion that the Lovecraftian being Dagon resides at the bottom, and that making sacrifices to the Deep Ones will bring them riches and power. Kids these days.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12108-gscrap","name":"gscrap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12108_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-17T21:29:40-07:00","id":933251,"title":"","content":"<b>120)</b> In a moment of whimsical boredom, the Band has decided to play a little game. They're attempting to create their own religion from the ground up, while boasting about the most ridiculously exaggerated legends they can come up with. If they were ordinary mortals, nobody would have taken them seriously. But they're not ordinary mortals, and now the Band has realized that a legitimate cult is beginning to form around them!<br /> <br /> The other pantheons refuse to give the Scions guidance in this manner, unless they renounce their false religion and pledge their loyalty back to their respective parents. But from the looks of things, the Scions might have the opportunity to break away from them and become their own pantheon. <i>So what's it going to be;</i> do you quit while you're ahead, or see how far this game escalates?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 07-18-2016, 12:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T18:38:33-07:00","id":936835,"title":"","content":"<b>121)</b> The Titans have done something they weren't supposed to do; they got smart! After repeatedly throwing waves of her children at Mount Olympus, Gaia has decided that if she can't attack the Overworld directly, then she shall do so indirectly. The prime avatar of Terra has begun to divert her forces to the World in hopes of destroying the mundane counterpart of the Theoi's home. Nobody is sure what will happen to the home of the Gods if that happens, but they don't intend to wait around and find out!<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>122)</b> When recounting the deeds of heroic figures, their more shady activities often get swept under the rug and fade from the public's collective knowledge. You have just heard rumors of a fellow Scion who seems to have let their heritage go to their heads and is behaving in a self aggrandizing manner which leads to innocent people getting hurt to satisfy their ego. Yet despite what you've heard, nobody seems to be prosecuting them; in fact, they're actually quite popular, despite their selfish behavior. And now you're starting to have some doubts yourself. Do you want to follow their example and lord your divine heritage over lesser mortals, or do you want to teach this Scion what it really means to be a hero?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T19:42:58-07:00","id":936859,"title":"","content":"123) To the Ancient Egyptians, the time before time was an endless void-ocean without shape or light until Ra hatched from his egg (or lotus, depending) to create the sun and bring forth dry land. This abyssal sea was represented by Nu, a frog-headed deity of the oldest Egyptian pantheon that was later forgotten. <br /> <br /> The thing is, Nu never died. It's a Titan, upset by all the light and sound and chaos of existence, and the time has finally come to make its move and return the world to nothing. Nu has servants and cultists searching for weapons of apocalyptic scope, but not even a nuclear holocaust erases things completely enough for its taste; it has placed its eyes squarely on the physics experiments conducted at the Large Hadron Collider and elsewhere, hoping to create a black hole that will engulf the World and return everything to the primordial nothingness. <br /> <br /> Nu is the oldest being, and one of the most patient; it has had thousands of years to build up a conspiracy of servants, and it falls to your band to stop the actually end of the universe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T06:43:27-07:00","id":938797,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>124)</b> Akhetaten's greatest strength is that it only has one Avatar, allowing it to marshal it's full army towards a singular purpose, without having to worry about conflicting ideas. But one Scion has come up with an extremely bold plan to change this uniformed cohesion by introducing a new Avatar for the Titan of Light. A sleeper agent who will combat Aten's forces from the inside out, and hopefully stem the tide of suicide bombers being sent into the Gods' territories. Of course, the Scion has generously volunteered to sacrifice himself to Akhetaten so that he may become the new Avatar, but his plans are met with great suspicion by the established pantheons. On one hand, not all Titans were considered dangerous enough to need to be sealed away, and it's possible that this Scion may prove to be one such example. But if something goes wrong with this plan, then the Gods will have one more enemy to worry about!<br /> <br /> The Scion does not seem to be the fool, however. They claim to have devised a ritual that will make the joining process go a lot smoother than it usually does. But when the players are petitioned by both sides of the argument, they must decide whether to help the Scion perform their ritual, or to disrupt its procedure and halt their ambitious plan.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 07-29-2016, 06:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T09:00:38-07:00","id":945486,"title":"","content":"<b>125)</b> Hermes, Loki, Set, Kalfu, tricksters and trouble makers all. And apparently Fate finds some perverse amusement in their antics, because it has conspired their children to come together in the same Band! The Gods are anxiously paranoid about what chaos these Scions might unleash as they travel the realms, building their Legends. But one thing's for sure, no other Band can piss off the Titans quite so artistically as them!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 08-07-2016, 06:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T22:43:43-07:00","id":945960,"title":"","content":"126) Okay, so there's this scion of Odin who got hanged by his own umbilical cord in the womb before being rescued by c-section, thus reenacting a certain ritual. The guy is a brilliant writer, has a few novel series, lives off the merch profits. Point is, his books are more than a little inspired by going ons in the titan war, which is why his latest work (and recent disappearance) has everyone a bit worried. Oh the title of the work?<i> In the Underworld of the Gods of the Neanderthals </i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T09:32:59-07:00","id":953885,"title":"","content":"<b>127)</b> Sooooo... attempting to seal all the Titans in New Tartarus with the ritual mask didn't pan out as well as we'd hoped. Most of the Avatars managed to escape, and Loki, ever the infuriating trickster, has now become the new Muspelheim when he used the Black Feather Shroud. The band of young Gods known as Harsihar, Adonis. Donner, Itztli Occelotl, Gimui Kuromizuhime, and Baronne De La Croix have decided they're not in the mood to deal with any more bullshit. They've done more than their fair share when they invaded and captured each of the prime avatars in their home realms. Now they deserve a vacation to rest and recover; so what do they do?<br /> <br /> Raise a new generation to take their place, of course! Each member of the Band has gone incognito and produced at least one Scion who they plan to grant a visitation when they come of age. The years have passed by, and the time approaches for a new generation of heroes to step into the spotlight and pick up where their parents left off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T23:06:40-07:00","id":956176,"title":"","content":"128) Okay, here's the thing, you know how the Christians and Muslims put the crucifixion around 29 AD? Well according to Plutarch, the same date that happened, there was a &quot;Great Howl&quot; announcing the death of Pan off the coast of the island of Corfu. You get what I am getting at here, right? That's right, Pan isn't just Satan, he's Jesus too. The whole religion is a scam Pan came up with to harness the power of the Abrahamic religions for Olympus before they became a threat to the gods. Just be careful about who you tell this too, the other pantheons weren't let in on this, and they would definitely want a cut of that action, which is why Pan has to pretend he is too weak to sire a scion...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T23:33:42-07:00","id":956179,"title":"","content":"129) The Dagda traditionally revives slain men with the butt of his club, and these are often his most powerful champions. It should come as no surprise when his newest Scion on the block happened to be dead last week, but Anpu caught wind of things and is fucking pissed; his freshest Scion, an ushabti given human life and appointed with the task of keeping the dead and the living wholly divided, is leading an all-out war effort on The Dagda's chosen. What should merely be a spat between two minor Scions at the behest of their gods has exploded into a massive conflict that threatens to engulf the city, with the traditional lords of the dead fighting against all of the deities of rebirth and resurrection, and the two Scions at the heart of the fighting don't even want to be there!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T14:53:22-07:00","id":962977,"title":"","content":"An ancient god of a long powerless pantheon kidnaps the infant children of other scions in order to create their own force of scions by way of forced adoption.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12349-evilnerf","name":"evilnerf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12349_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T08:27:57-07:00","id":971939,"title":"","content":"131) <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HyTIt4AioEI\" data-code=\"HyTIt4AioEI\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/HyTIt4AioEI/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T08:39:42-07:00","id":971943,"title":"","content":"132) A multitude of gods associated with celestial bodies, especially the sun, have started to go missing and nobody has any idea why. A member of your Band (or a Scion friend of your Band) ended up using Mystery to try and find out. The only answer they got was this:<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">The Fifth Sun is Hungry.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12300,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","user":"Crying","date":". 09-23-2016, 03:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","name":"Crying","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12300_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T10:04:15-07:00","id":971982,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>133)</b> Okay, there's surpassing your parent's expectations, and then there's trying too hard. This is a case of the latter, as one of Zeus' children has decided to one up his father's reputation as one of the biggest sex-aholics in history. All he has to do is fuck the planet... No, I mean actually <i>fuck the planet</i>... Yes, that's right, the thing you're standing on!<br /> <br /> Well I don't know how he plans to do it! A giant's toy, a magic spell, some long forgotten Avatar?<br /> <br /> Look the important thing is he's planning to do inappropriate things to the earth, and I don't think all that slamming, grinding and smacking is going to be good for the environment, much less the people who live here. And as if that wasn't enough, the<i> 'white sea'</i> will probably drown any survivors left in its wake.<br /> <br /> Tell your Band to suit up, because it looks like you're about to perform a <i>Legendary</i> cock block!</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-18-2016, 01:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T17:40:17-07:00","id":972233,"title":"","content":"134) One of the players parent gods has an asteroid or planet that is associated to them (Such as Zeus and Jupiter). However, NASA has decided to send a probe to the planet, with the name of a rival god attached to it. The parent god, feeling petty, asks their scion to sabotage the probe in a dramatic fashion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12349,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12349-evilnerf","user":"evilnerf","date":". 09-22-2016, 11:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12349-evilnerf","name":"evilnerf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12349_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T19:40:59-07:00","id":974824,"title":"","content":"<b>135)</b> There's trouble on campus. A an exclusive fraternity of Satanists have recently stolen a Scion's book of spells and have been using forbidden arts to transform their members into satyrs, whom they believe to be actual devils. The ritual is very complex, and they only have enough time to transform a few members each night before the sun rises. But once they have successfully transformed the entire fraternity, they plan to throw the biggest party of the century, turning the entire campus into rabid, frothing maniacs! A simple noise complaint isn't going to get them to stop, and the cops would most likely be torn to shreds by the psychotic Maenads they've rounded up for &quot;entertainment.&quot; <br /> <br /> No, unfortunately, you're going to have to crash the festivities (preferably before they start) and force them to disband their fraternity completely!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T14:02:50-07:00","id":977959,"title":"","content":"136) The City of Angels is a shining light in an America tired from war, and the heroes of the screen make their magic on her whims and will. But while YHVH and his angels have their hooks in the police force, both His pride and the force's biases leave the various ethnic neighborhoods to fend for themselves; the other Pantheons run their people as criminal rackets and petty cults, and the whole city threatens to boil over. Can your Band cross the cultural lines and organize some spirit of cooperation - or will they try to take the whole shebang for themselves?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T20:49:17-07:00","id":988663,"title":"","content":"137: Every day, Horus rides the rails across the heavens, driving the solar steam engine out of the night and up above the world, and every day, Set pics up his gun and buries his grudges to ride his horse right alongside the tracks. The two of them hate each other, but the only thing they hate more is that no-good rattler Apep, who wants to wrap the train up in his coils and eat the sun whole. The old myths always did tell the Netjer to head West, and there's only really one desert if you look at the world the right way...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T07:14:57-07:00","id":988847,"title":"","content":"138: A disgruntled employee of the World Wide Web Consortium notices the beginnings of a strange symbol in the construction of code in global internet protocols. Rather than correct it, they complete it using knowledge of old Norse runic script and transfer the data to an unsuspecting server farm to implement as a test run. The result is lines of power bending and taking shape to something hideous; a creature born of anger and frustration and given form by code and electricity: An Internet Troll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T03:15:57-07:00","id":989272,"title":"","content":"139:a forgotten irish titan, &quot;the mother (in celtic)&quot;, starts raising a bunch of childrens of the gods, kidnapping the babies in their cradles. After the brainwash the scion will be raised with a single purpose: Revenge against the irish gods who destroyed the children's titan, in the name of the lovely mother","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12508-elanconnor","name":"ElanConnor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12508_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T22:53:12-08:00","id":1000160,"title":"","content":"<b>140)</b> It was supposed to be a joke, a game played by children to scare each other silly. In any other circumstance, it might have been just that, but unfortunately for you, you're a Scion. And Fate doesn't just let that kind of stuff slide. Now, you're being haunted by Daruma San, a famous specter of Japan, and you've only got 24 hours to catch her... Before she catches you!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T00:53:27-08:00","id":1000653,"title":"","content":"141) The Yankees won't shut up about their election and all the other Pantheons are sick of hearing them talk about it. [INSERT DIVINE PARENT HERE] has asked you and your group to make them shut up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","name":"Crying","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12300_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T01:02:56-08:00","id":1001666,"title":"","content":"142) Your pantheon's monarch/chief/parent-and-progenitor has asked you (and, by extension, your Band) to play matchmaker for the Scions of two other deities from your pantheon. Specifically, two deities with a history of enmity/estrangement between them. (Naturally, this works best if at least one of those Scions is already in your player group.)<br /> <br /> According to the requestee, dark days are coming, for the World in general, and your pantheon specifically. The theory is that this marriage will begin healing the metaphysical breach between the feuding gods, and help your pantheon with some much-needed unity. Of course, the good making this request isn't always known for clarity or sanity (monarch/chief/parent-and-progenitor deities often aren't.) But they might just be right this time...<br /> <br /> (This is based on a storyline my own gaming group began to play out, between my Scion of Tsuki-yomi and another player's Scion of Amaterasu. Sadly, that player quit the game almost immediately thereafter, so it went nowhere. Hopefully, you'll have better luck...)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12628-yukikaze","name":"yukikaze","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T06:55:31-08:00","id":1001740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>yukikaze</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/431083-101-scion-story-hooks?p=1001666#post1001666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(This is based on a storyline my own gaming group began to play out, between my Scion of Tsuki-yomi and another player's Scion of Amaterasu. Sadly, that player quit the game almost immediately thereafter, so it went nowhere. Hopefully, you'll have better luck...)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Amaterasu and Tsuki-Yomi are siblings. <i>That made the Scions cousins.</i> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T09:34:23-08:00","id":1001807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/431083-101-scion-story-hooks?p=1001740#post1001740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Amaterasu and Tsuki-Yomi are siblings. <i>That made the Scions cousins.</i> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Amaterasu and Tsukuyomi are also (formerly) married. That makes the Scions ... whatever that makes them, it's kinda icky <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos","name":"Sacerdos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10624_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"231"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T09:35:15-08:00","id":1001808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/431083-101-scion-story-hooks?p=1001740#post1001740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Amaterasu and Tsuki-Yomi are siblings. <i>That made the Scions cousins.</i> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>We were well aware. Not the most eyebrow-raising thing that happened in that campaign.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sacerdos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/431083-101-scion-story-hooks?p=1001807#post1001807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Amaterasu and Tsukuyomi are also (formerly) married. That makes the Scions ... whatever that makes them, it's kinda icky <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>*That* we didn't become aware of until well after the campaign ended. Even so, it struck us that sibling marriages and other incestuous instances were common enough in mythology that cousins... well, cousin-ish people getting romantic was relatively tame.<br /> <br /> ***<br /> <br /> 143) Some say that we are fated to become our parents. And in recent months, Scions are starting to experience that fated-ness (with a capital &quot;F&quot;). Those who try to be different than their divine parents (kind in comparison to cruel, altruistic in comparison to self-absorbed, et cetera) find themselves drawn, like moths to a flame, to that same kind of behavior. Ditto for their powers: woe betide the Scion of a fire god who tries to use his Water purview.<br /> <br /> Your Band is relatively unaffected so far, and so you lot have been &quot;requested&quot; to get to the bottom of this. And fast, before you find yourselves reliving your parents' mistakes indefinitely.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12628,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12628-yukikaze","user":"yukikaze","date":". 11-11-2016, 02:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12628-yukikaze","name":"yukikaze","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T14:07:48-08:00","id":1001931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>yukikaze</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/431083-101-scion-story-hooks?p=1001808#post1001808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> *That* we didn't become aware of until well after the campaign ended. Even so, it struck us that sibling marriages and other incestuous instances were common enough in mythology that cousins... well, cousin-ish people getting romantic was relatively tame.<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I've been told incest is actually quite common among the Egyptian pantheon.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>144) </b>When it comes to family feuds, it seems Fate has a hard on for them. Almost immediately after your visitation, you received a Fate Bond that has existed since time beyond mortal reckoning. Your divine bloodline, and that of another deity, are destined to oppose each other until the end of time. It just so happens that another Scion received their visitation around the same time you did, and now they find themselves compelled to challenge you at every opportunity. Regardless of the motives or cause, they just feel compelled to stand against your side of the argument. Maybe that wouldn't be as terrible as it sounds, if they didn't have a plan to break the fate bond. It's a simple process of killing the rival bloodline before they produce the next generation to perpetuate the cycle. That's right, your new rival isn't content to just sit back and act as a foil to your schemes in some grand tapestry, they're determined to make their own destiny, but they need you out of the way to do it.<br /> <br /> Luckily for you, two can play at that game!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T20:26:38-08:00","id":1002451,"title":"","content":"<b>145)</b> Ah-Muzen-Cab has always been something of a mystery to everybody, even his own pantheon. The rest of the K'uh have no records of him, he sort of just showed up one day and declared himself to be the god of bees to the Mayans. Given his general benevolance, the K'uh decided to allow him to join, though his refusal to tell them of his past has often been a source of contention.<br /> <br /> However, recently, a depiction of the Bacab by the Mud-men of the First World has been uncovered by some enterprising young Scions and one of them bears a suspicious resemblance to the bee god...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12300,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","user":"Crying","date":".  Cleaning it up 11-13-2016, 01:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","name":"Crying","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12300_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-13T21:51:37-08:00","id":1002769,"title":"","content":"<b>145)</b> If this is somebody's idea of a prank, you really don't understand the joke. Every night, you awaken to the sound of croaking outside your door, which does not cease until you go to investigate. But every time you do, you find a bullfrog sitting on the other side of the door, staring motionless at you. Each time you dispose of it, the frog seems to grow a little bigger than last time. Until finally, it's reached Nemean proportions and its croaking is loud enough to sound like moaning wails. You should probably take care of this, or your warty friend might reach Typhonian status before too long!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T14:05:46-08:00","id":1003051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/431083-101-scion-story-hooks?p=1002769#post1002769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>145)</b> Every night, you awaken to the sound of croaking outside your door, which does not cease until you go to investigate. But every time you do, you find a bullfrog sitting on the other side of the door, staring motionless at you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please tell me it's croaking like this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/pVcbasIb8lQ\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/pVcbasIb8lQ\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/pVcbasIb8lQ\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/pVcbasIb8lQ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> * * *<br /> <br /> 146) Competition and oneupsmanship are nothing new to the gods.<br /> <br /> The latest fad: street racing!<br /> <br /> Perhaps Thor is a bit too enamored of <i>Days of Thunder</i>, or Indra finds common ground with movies that are fast and furious. But neither deities nor their offspring are immune to adrenaline rushes or counting coup at each other's expense, and the chosen racetracks aren't hairpin curves on mountain roads. No, we're talking treacherous courses winding through Terrae Incognita or Underworlds... without the local flora or fauna being cordoned off for drivers' safety.<br /> <br /> Now, the various pantheons are sponsoring a major competition for their Scions, through the most treacherous course yet, and your Band has been &quot;volunteered&quot; to participate! The prizes: tricked-out relic muscle cars made by the forge-gods themselves. But before you start salivating, remember the &quot;most treacherous course yet&quot; part!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12628,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12628-yukikaze","user":"yukikaze","date":". 11-19-2016, 01:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12628-yukikaze","name":"yukikaze","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T14:34:04-08:00","id":1003072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>yukikaze</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/431083-101-scion-story-hooks?p=1003051#post1003051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> 146) Competition and oneupsmanship are nothing new to the gods.<br /> <br /> The latest fad: street racing!<br /> <br /> Perhaps Thor is a bit too enamored of Days of Thunder, or Indra finds common ground with movies that are fast and furious. But neither deities nor their offspring are immune to adrenaline rushes or counting coup at each other's expense, and the chosen racetracks aren't hairpin curves on mountain roads. No, we're talking treacherous courses winding through Terrae Incognita or Underworlds... without the local flora or fauna being cordoned off for drivers' safety.<br /> <br /> Now, the various pantheons are sponsoring a major competition for their Scions, through the most treacherous course yet, and your Band has been &quot;volunteered&quot; to participate! The prizes: tricked-out relic muscle cars made by the forge-gods themselves. But before you start salivating, remember the &quot;most treacherous course yet&quot; part!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Valhalla awaits!<br /> <br /> Witness me!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T14:57:38-08:00","id":1003085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/431083-101-scion-story-hooks?p=1003072#post1003072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Valhalla awaits!<br /> <br /> Witness me!</div> </div> </div> </div>Meanwhile, Eric Donner actually manages a midair drift, because stormcloud tires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12628-yukikaze","name":"yukikaze","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T11:55:19-08:00","id":1003519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>yukikaze</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/431083-101-scion-story-hooks?p=1003051#post1003051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 146) Competition and oneupsmanship are nothing new to the gods.<br /> <br /> The latest fad: street racing!<br /> <br /> Perhaps Thor is a bit too enamored of Days of Thunder, or Indra finds common ground with movies that are fast and furious. But neither deities nor their offspring are immune to adrenaline rushes or counting coup at each other's expense, and the chosen racetracks aren't hairpin curves on mountain roads. No, we're talking treacherous courses winding through Terrae Incognita or Underworlds... without the local flora or fauna being cordoned off for drivers' safety.<br /> <br /> Now, the various pantheons are sponsoring a major competition for their Scions, through the most treacherous course yet, and your Band has been &quot;volunteered&quot; to participate! The prizes: tricked-out relic muscle cars made by the forge-gods themselves. But before you start salivating, remember the &quot;most treacherous course yet&quot; part!</div> </div> </div> </div>Lovely idea. Cinematic as all heck, too. Bravo.<br /> ... Hopefully, Pelops and Phaeton aren't participating? Nobody in their right mind would go anywhere near those two and a vehicle.<br /> Unless somebody wanted to make things especially exciting. (Trickster gods: &quot;because we can&quot; is a perfectly valid reason for anything! )<br /> Btw, are bets allowed? Because I kind of expect the Ashvins to win this.<br /> (meanwhile, the Mexica gods are very pissed, because wheels are just not. their. thing. Not that they wanted any part of that competition, of course...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5530,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5530-xanthias","user":"Xanthias","date":". 11-16-2016, 02:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5530-xanthias","name":"Xanthias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T21:13:12-08:00","id":1003770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xanthias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/431083-101-scion-story-hooks?p=1003519#post1003519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lovely idea. Cinematic as all heck, too. Bravo.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. I'll admit, I was thinking of this scene:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/NmuhDELwH8E\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/NmuhDELwH8E\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/NmuhDELwH8E\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/NmuhDELwH8E </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> (And every Band has at least one Scion who'd probably try to pull the &quot;no thanks, I choose life&quot; routine, and end up having to be pushed...)<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xanthias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/431083-101-scion-story-hooks?p=1003519#post1003519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless somebody wanted to make things especially exciting. (Trickster gods: &quot;because we can&quot; is a perfectly valid reason for anything! )</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to mention the gods who would say &quot;if you're not cheating, you're not trying.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12628-yukikaze","name":"yukikaze","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T22:59:06-08:00","id":1003793,"title":"","content":"<b>147)</b> So yeah, you remember rumors about how the Statue of Liberty is a sleeping colossus? Well it seems that somebody finally managed to wake the old girl up, and then sent her on a rampage. Lady Liberty is invoking her namesake by destroying the newly built prisons meant to hold Titanspawn, apparently having mistaken them to be oppressed individuals. To make matters even worse, her torch and book (both of which are welded into her grasp) allow her to channel the Fire, Guardian and Justice perviews, which makes a head on confrontation with her a very poor decision. You need to find the one controlling the big, green lady and compel her to return to her post before you're forced to destroy a national monument!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 11-16-2016, 02:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T03:52:07-08:00","id":1003849,"title":"","content":"<b>147.5)</b> Hey, so remember the rumors about Christ the Redeemer also being a collosus? Well, let's just say that Jesus wants a hug.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12300,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","user":"Crying","date":".  Also, he isn't happy about all these damn Pagan gods running around and fucking with humanity, but that really is secondary to the hug. 11-16-2016, 06:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","name":"Crying","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12300_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T00:19:29-08:00","id":1004278,"title":"","content":"<b>147.75) </b>Continuing with this colossal theme:<br /> <br /> The Daibutsu statue at K\u014dtoku-in (immortalized in Kipling's &quot;The Buddha at Kamukura&quot;) has also begun acting in an irregular fashion.<br /> <br /> And by &quot;irregular,&quot; I mean &quot;moving around and crushing things.&quot;<br /> <br /> Oh, and while you're putting a spike in its rampaging? The Kami with Buddhist associations would appreciate you returning it to Kamakura relatively intact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12628,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12628-yukikaze","user":"yukikaze","date":". 11-17-2016, 03:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12628-yukikaze","name":"yukikaze","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T14:42:58-08:00","id":1004640,"title":"","content":"<b>148)</b> Your childhood friend got a new dog that he just adores to death, and wants to show it off to you. Unfortunately, the moment you're alone with the dog, it points to you with one paw and says &quot;tonight... you&quot; in a menacing voice. It turns out that your friend has somehow managed to obtain a Fenrir mutt, having mistaken it for some kind of wolf-dog. They're completely oblivious to its supernatural origins, and trying to explain it to them would not go over well, seeing as how you've kept your true heritage a secret all this time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T05:01:51-08:00","id":1005309,"title":"","content":"<b>149)</b> Zeus isn't known for his conventional wisdom, but when it came to forbidding humans to have access to fire, he may have had a point. After it was discovered, the use of fire became so integral to humanity, that civilization can no longer survive without Muspelheim's continued support. Unfortunately, the Theoi's contempt for mortals is well established, as is Zeus' tyrannical selfishness. He's finally decided to take out Prometheus for good, and damn the consequences!<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, destroying the avatar of creativity would spell disaster throughout all facets of mortal society, and the other pantheons can't allow that. They're not particularly happy about it, but it seems this time, the scions must protect a Titan from an attack by the Gods, Well, <i>first time for everything</i>, as they say.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T19:16:31-08:00","id":1005540,"title":"","content":"<i>Recommended for established Scions (Legend 4+):</i><br /> <br /> <b>150)</b> It's as true for the divine world as for the mundane one: the reward for a job well done is more work, usually harder and less pleasant. So, when your pantheon's head asks you (as an up-and-comer) to show his newest Visited Scion the ropes, you already know that &quot;honor&quot; is a dubious one.<br /> <br /> It gets worse.<br /> <br /> You see, you already know this new Scion. It's your cousin, a spoiled brat and troublemaker whom you've always had to bail out (and who's never had an ounce of gratitude for it). And finding out they're half-God hasn't done a damned thing for developing their humility or willingness to work with people.<br /> <br /> So. If something happens to this jerk, you're gonna get it from both your mundane and divine families. Your requirement to watch after them is likely to try your Bandmates' patience. And your cousin wouldn't follow directions even if Zeus zapped them directly into their brain.<br /> <br /> Better ask your Band's resident brain to gin up some celestial-strength ibuprofen for you. You're gonna need it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12628,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12628-yukikaze","user":"yukikaze","date":". 11-20-2016, 01:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12628-yukikaze","name":"yukikaze","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T10:56:58-08:00","id":1006284,"title":"","content":"<b>151)</b> For as long as either of you can remember, your sister has always wanted to be famous, but while she did have some latent talent, she never seemed to attract the talent scouts and make it big. That is until last week when she calls you up and says she finally hit the big one, somebody had finally recognized her potential and offered her a contract deal. She'd be on her way to stardom the next time you heard from her!<br /> <br /> But then something happened last night. Astronomers found a brand new constellation that seemed to appear in the sky out of nowhere. After they finished mapping out the constellation and presented it to the public, you noticed it bares a striking resemblance to your sister, who has thus far cut off all contact with you and the rest of the family...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 11-21-2016, 01:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T01:25:27-08:00","id":1009232,"title":"","content":"<b>152) </b>Stonehenge is no stranger to mystery and myth. Lately, however, people and creatures with Legendary aspects to them have been drawn to it, more than normal. It's almost as if it has become a celestial leak that supernatural is seeping through, enough so that even mundane tourists are picking up on it. Your Band has been &quot;requested&quot; to investigate, and to do so without treading on the toes of the local deities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12628-yukikaze","name":"yukikaze","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T03:07:47-08:00","id":1009256,"title":"","content":"<b>153)</b> It finally happened. Humanity discovered intelligent life in outer space - we found aliens! However, while the insectoid beings have opened up peaceful relations and seem nice enough, the same cannot be said for their ancient, incomprehensible deities...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","name":"Crying","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12300_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T09:45:14-08:00","id":1009374,"title":"","content":"<b>154)</b> Two schools of thought have emerged among the Scions of the World. One side claims that it is their duty to protect and serve, while the other claims it is their right to conquer and rule. Fate, it seems, has just pulled an X-Men, and a vast number of Scions are being drawn to one faction or the other as they decide how they wish to use their divine powers. Neither school has thrown in with the Titans, as they both still aid the side of the Gods, but their ideologies on what it means to be a Scion are mutually exclusive to each other. They can not both get what they want, and so they have turned on each other in an effort to convert or dispose of as many members of the opposite side as possible, before this escalates into full blown war.<br /> <br /> And as newly visited Scions, you are wild cards in this debate. They will come to recruit you soon, and at least one of them isn't likely to accept 'no' for an answer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T13:04:23-08:00","id":1009443,"title":"","content":"<b>155) </b>It's common enough for Scions to resent their godly parents. After all, many deities have a rep for being lousy moms and dads (even to their fully-divine kids).<br /> <br /> A Scion with a social-media following who calls out those divine deadbeats in song form? That's new. And alarming, given that the songs are going viral.<br /> <br /> It's up to you and your Band to play damage control, before this becomes a trend among disaffected Scions (and gives the Titans a wedge they can exploit). Keep in mind, though, that the frame of mind that led to this is something that will probably require more than just a quick fix.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12628,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12628-yukikaze","user":"yukikaze","date":". 11-28-2016, 04:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12628-yukikaze","name":"yukikaze","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T13:42:54-08:00","id":1009467,"title":"","content":"<b>156)</b> There has been a coup, Zeus has been toppled from his throne and Athena now rules Olympus in his place. But what's even more shocking is that now everybody knows why Athena was so adamant about remaining a virgin. It turns out that <i>she's a he</i>, having disguised their identity all this time until they were ready to fulfill the prophecy and overthrow their father. Like the past two monarchs before him, Zeus was castrated by his traitorous offspring, stripping him of his potency in more ways than one. Now, Olympus is in an uproar as the 'goddess' of wisdom is imposing new social reform policies throughout the entire religion, and the children of the Theoi are getting dragged into the mix!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 11-28-2016, 09:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T21:36:35-08:00","id":1009635,"title":"","content":"<b>157) </b>In the mists of ancient Finnish mythohistory, the Sampo -- the great artifact forged by Ilmarinen to bring prosperity to his people -- was lost, believed destroyed. Now rumors are rising of a nearly identical relic, bringing fortune and wealth to an enterprising group of titanspawn. It's not clear if this is the recovered original Sampo, or if these titanspawn have forced a craftsman of Ilmarinen's talent to make a new one. What is clear is that they can't be allowed to keep it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12628-yukikaze","name":"yukikaze","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T10:04:54-08:00","id":1009839,"title":"","content":"<b>158)</b> Excalibur, from the united king. He's looking for him, he's going to California!<br /> <br /> And so is everybody else who thinks they have a shot at becoming the true king of Britain!<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>159)</b> Do you like giant robot battles? Because the Titans have been constructing the biggest one ever seen. A colossus of such enormous size it requires not one, but six pilots working in unison to operate it properly. Construction is only weeks away from completion and the pantheons are getting nervous. It's up to you to track down the facility and destroy it before they finish their work. Or, on the other hand, you and your Band could steal it for yourself!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T02:34:13-08:00","id":1010558,"title":"","content":"<b>160)</b> There's good news and there's bad news. The good news is that your childhood friend has been discovered to also be a Scion - they're the reincarnation of Cu Chulainn! You can go on adventures and spend time with them just like old times, it will be great! The bad news is that the Morrigan was the one to discover this, and it is unlikely that she will leave Cu's reincarnation alone...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","name":"Crying","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12300_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T05:14:25-08:00","id":1010582,"title":"","content":"<i>My birthday was yesterday. I'm 29 now.</i><br /> <br /> <b>161)</b> The month of October, the time when the barrier between this world and the ones beyond is weakened and magic becomes easier to cast. Normally, the spirit of Jack-o-Lantern patrols the world during this time to scare off malicious spirits who seek to threaten the good folk of the world. But he's been incapacitated this year and forced to hand his duties off to a substitute. Which just so happens to be you! Donning the mantle of the pumpkin king, your job is to make sure the barrier between worlds is kept in check, because the Titanspawn are seeing this as an opportunity to kick open the doors to New Tartarus!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T05:39:06-08:00","id":1010589,"title":"","content":"<b>162) </b>Hawaii here we Come! Or Not. After getting plane tickets to honolulu as your new christmas present you find out the hotel you were going to be staying at has been closed due to white-out conditions. However as a free bonus the captain of a new cruise resort has promised a 3 night stay on his ship as repayment. The trouble is that the captain's name is Maui and there are a few legendary creatures not happy with his return to the sea...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/885-bwgustaf","name":"bwgustaf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T13:59:52-08:00","id":1010804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crying</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/431083-101-scion-story-hooks?p=1010558#post1010558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>160)</b> There's good news and there's bad news. The good news is that your childhood friend has been discovered to also be a Scion - they're the reincarnation of Cu Chulainn! You can go on adventures and spend time with them just like old times, it will be great! The bad news is that the Morrigan was the one to discover this, and it is unlikely that she will leave Cu's reincarnation alone...</div> </div> </div> </div><b>160b)</b> The other bad news is that the Morrigan is your(or one of your Bandmate's) mother.<br /> <br /> So yeah, have fun with that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://s3.amazonaws.com/ksr/avatars/3507685/Exalted_Back.small.jpg?1370109312\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <hr />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/446-nervaqus987","name":"Nervaqus987","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar446_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T19:45:23-08:00","id":1010908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/431083-101-scion-story-hooks?p=1010582#post1010582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>My birthday was yesterday. I'm 29 now.</i><br /> <br /> <b>161)</b> The month of October, the time when the barrier between this world and the ones beyond is weakened and magic becomes easier to cast. Normally, the spirit of Jack-o-Lantern patrols the world during this time to scare off malicious spirits who seek to threaten the good folk of the world. But he's been incapacitated this year and forced to hand his duties off to a substitute. Which just so happens to be you! Donning the mantle of the pumpkin king, your job is to make sure the barrier between worlds is kept in check, because the Titanspawn are seeing this as an opportunity to kick open the doors to New Tartarus!</div> </div> </div> </div>Happy birthday!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","name":"Crying","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12300_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T22:55:25-08:00","id":1010948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/431083-101-scion-story-hooks?p=1010582#post1010582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>My birthday was yesterday. I'm 29 now.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Happy birthday!<br /> <br /> <b>163) </b>Freyr's lost sword was has been found! Naturally enough, the person who's found it has no idea of its divine origins. Instead, they're an indie filmmaker who thinks the &quot;fighting on its own&quot; ability is just some nifty, high-tech feature that'll be perfect for his new science-fantasy masterpiece. (He's even got a noted voice-actor to &quot;play&quot; the sword.) <br /> <br /> Of course, he has no idea why his cast and crew keep getting attacked by weirdos lately. Good luck explaining it to him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12628-yukikaze","name":"yukikaze","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T01:30:50-08:00","id":1010976,"title":"","content":"<b>164)</b> So it turns out that Santa Claus is one of Big Papa One Eye's (Odin's) Mantles. Through it he's managed to stay relevant even as the worship of the rest of his pantheon declined. He even manages to not be a complete asshole sometimes thanks to it! Unfortunately, someone has taken on the Mantle of Krampus. That someone being a rather large wolf with a grudge against Odin for his imprisonment...<br /> <br /> It seems unlikely that Fenrir will stick to just punishing naughty children this Christmas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12300,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","user":"Crying","date":". 03-13-2020, 09:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","name":"Crying","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12300_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T05:37:45-08:00","id":1011025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crying</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/431083-101-scion-story-hooks?p=1010976#post1010976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>164)</b> So it turns out that Santa Claus is one of Big Papa One Eye's Mantles. Throught it he's managed to stay relevant even as the worship of the rest of his pantheon declined. He even manages to not be a complete asshole sometimes thanks to it! Unfortunately, someone has taken on the Mantle of Krampus. That someone being a rather large wolf with a grudge against Odin for his imprisonement...<br /> <br /> It seems unlikely that Fenrir will stick to just punishing naughty children this Christmas.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> (and it seems nobody told the wolf that Crampus is supposed to be a goat <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>165)</b> Ah, Thanksgiving! A time in which the American people celebrate the day the pilgrims came together and broke bread with the natives. Most people today like to conveniently ignore the events that came afterward, or just move straight on to thinking about Christmas. Well, the Gods are not most people, and they have very, very long memories. Every year around this time, tensions run high between the Yankee pantheon and the spiritual deities of the native cultures, with the Scions being the ones stuck in the middle. Well, not this time, you say! We're going to have a proper thanksgiving festival, and this time we're inviting the gods to sit down and clear the air between them!<br /> <br /> Just don't think about the fact that some of the Yankees might have actually taken part in the massacres prior to their apotheosis...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 12-02-2016, 02:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T17:25:11-08:00","id":1011281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/431083-101-scion-story-hooks?p=1011025#post1011025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(and it seems nobody told the wolf that Crampus is supposed to be a goat <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)</div> </div> </div> </div>Little know fact, Fenrir is a master at cosplaying. He can even make himself look like a convincing goat!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","name":"Crying","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12300_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T22:58:43-08:00","id":1011873,"title":"","content":"<b>166)</b> Titanspawn are getting pissed off... more so than usual. It was all fun and games when the Gods and Scions were the only ones who worried about Fatebonds, but now even the self respecting monsters are getting screwed over by mortals! We are, of course, referring to the creatures of the night (vampires, werewolves, ghosts, est). They used to be horrifying, causing mortals to lock their doors and windows at night, praying the monsters weren't already inside the house. But now, some asshole Scions in charge of public broadcasting have been spinning the stories of how the creatures are brooding, misunderstood individuals who just want to be loved. <i>I</i><i>t's disgusting</i>, and an insult to to the pride of the Titanspawn and their servants!<br /> <br /> But the greatest threat of all isn't that the Gods are trying to humiliate these monsters, it's that they're trying to recruit them! The plan is to humanize the Titanspawn as much as possible, and effectively sever their connection to the Greater Titans, just like the humans once did for the Gods.<br /> <br /> This can not stand. It's time mortals remembered what true fear is. The creatures of darkness are about to step into the light, and when they do, mortals will be praying like hell that they go back to whence they came!<br /> <br /> (A reverse chronicle in which you play as servants of the Titans)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 12-04-2016, 02:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T10:24:10-08:00","id":1012061,"title":"","content":"<b>167)</b> The thu'um, he has the thu'um! Well, okay, it's actually just a new Strength knack he developed that allows him to roar with the force of a shockwave. So when he went around claiming he was Dovahkiin, everybody had a good laugh. That is until the sky above Mt. Everest opened up and a huge black dragon flew out of it. They call themselves the World Eater, and the Valkyries have been unable to do their jobs because an impenetrable fog has rolled into Valhalla!<br /> <br /> Enough with the jokes, an army of European dragons have sworn themselves to the World Eater's banner and descended upon the race of mortals. It's open season on dragon hunting for the duration of this crisis. Unfortunately, the only way to stop all of this is for the self proclaimed Dovahkiin to fulfill the obligations of their Fatebond and slay the World Eater in personal combat!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T01:15:38-08:00","id":1013632,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\">A continuation of 153. Sort of, anyway...<br /> <br /> <b>168)</b> Humanity has been at war with the <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">\u00c6skril, the second alien species they ever met, for the last twenty years now. They've made huge technological leaps during the war and, with the help of the first alien species they ever met, the Ya'natuk, victory seems like a real possibility. The same cannot be said for the gods, however. While the Ya'natuk have allied themselves with the humans in this war, their gods allied with the </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u00c6skril pantheon and while they have managed to hold out so far, the future looks dim.<br /> <br /> The only way it could get worse is if the Titans were to break out...</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","name":"Crying","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12300_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T07:15:28-08:00","id":1013736,"title":"","content":"<b>169)</b> A thorough study of the Greco-Roman pantheon reveals that the gods held very different personalities and roles between which culture they were depicted in. It's almost as if they were two different people. Well, turns out that's exactly right, because Fate has decided to whip up not one, but two sets of Olympians, and neither pantheon is happy about this arrangement. Olympus has erupted into a civil war, with the gods of Greece and Rome struggling for dominance while Terra plans her next assault. Something needs to be done about this horrendously disastrous Fatebond in order to restore order to Olympus. Or the next time Terra invades the mountain paradise, they won't have the strength to stop her!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T22:41:59-08:00","id":1014173,"title":"","content":"<b>170)</b> Do you know what's weird? The fact that Titanspawn are still viewed as Legendary beings by most people and not as real creatures. I mean, okay sure, awareness of their realness is being raised now that the Titans have been released and they're setting their minions loose, but it's not like there weren't Titanspawn already in the World before.<br /> <br /> The Titans being locked up and the Gods not coming down to the world anymore shouldn't have stopped the Titanspawn from going around and doing what they were doing before, right? Hell, shouldn't it have given them more incentive, since the gods weren't making any Scions to stop them?<br /> <br /> No, there must have been something stopping the Titanspawn from being known in the World... and I think I know what it is. Have you ever heard of the motto <i>Secure</i>, <i>Contain</i>, <i>Protect </i>before..?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","name":"Crying","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12300_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T23:44:00-08:00","id":1014190,"title":"","content":"<b>171)</b> So a relatively minor deity in your pantheon is trying to raise their public profile (and hopefully their Legend) through media based (loosely) upon their adventures. Movies, comics, and the like are certainly a viable way to get your name and face out there.<br /> <br /> Problem is, these works are starting to associate the god in question with powers and adventures that are rightfully associated with other gods. They're taking notice, and they aren't happy to share the stage with a &quot;lesser&quot; deity. Time to smooth ruffled feathers before things get tetchy (and by &quot;tetchy,&quot; we mean &quot;divine lightning bolts&quot;).<br /> <br /> <b>172)</b> Everyone knows that death isn't necessarily the final word when you're a god. Not that that overcoming it is a cakewalk.<br /> <br /> One of the long-deceased deities from your pantheon is in need of resurrection. The resident god of prophecy claims their presence will be vital to victory over your pantheon's foes. So, lucky you -- your &quot;final exam&quot; for advancement to godhood is to restore one of these deceased deities.<br /> <br /> No word about how you're supposed to do that, or what the dead god's former rivals are likely to do about it (note to self: do <i>not</i> invite Tsukuyomi to Uke-Mochi's welcome-back banquet)... if you want to be a god, this is the kind of thing you have to deal with...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12628,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12628-yukikaze","user":"yukikaze","date":". 08-26-2017, 12:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12628-yukikaze","name":"yukikaze","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T18:20:46-08:00","id":1014560,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>173) </b><i><span style=\"color:#000000\">Come down to Lake Pontchartrain.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Rest your soul and feed your brain.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Free for you and all your friends</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Craw fish 'til the bitter end.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Come down to Lake Pontchartrain.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Wade to where the shallows break.</span></i></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:DroidSansRegular\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><i>That's where you will get to see<br /> Everything the water can be.</i><br /> <br /> So some weird stuff has been going down at Lake Pontchartrain. Radio signals, with no origin, are advertising it to people within a 3 mile radius. People claim to be hearing voices coming from beneath the lake. And then there's the whole thing about the lake opening up and swallowing people...</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12300,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","user":"Crying","date":". 12-08-2016, 09:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","name":"Crying","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12300_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T13:11:16-08:00","id":1015347,"title":"","content":"<b>174) </b>How many Scions make it to demigodhood, let alone apotheosis, with their sanity intact? The number is lower than anyone is comfortable with.<br /> <br /> But even an insane Scion who's been Visited and empowered is too useful a weapon to leave sitting on the sidelines. It's sad, but some gods see it as a brutal necessity. So, these Scions have begun to be employed as sentient weapons of mass destruction on the battlefield, in loose &quot;Bands&quot; with several relatively stable Scions trying to ride herd on them.<br /> <br /> Guess what you and your buddies have been volunteered for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12628,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12628-yukikaze","user":"yukikaze","date":". 12-10-2016, 05:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12628-yukikaze","name":"yukikaze","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T20:54:59-08:00","id":1017935,"title":"","content":"<b>175) </b>Everybody knows that kisses have magical properties, particularly the ability to break curses. The kiss of a princess can undo metamorphosis spells, true love's first kiss can undo sleep or mind control spells, etc...<br /> <br /> The thing that's puzzling you is that last you checked, you were slowly dying from a curse and the only other person in this cave with you is your rival. How come you feel better now..?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12300,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","user":"Crying","date":".  Phrasing 12-15-2016, 11:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","name":"Crying","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12300_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T05:50:23-08:00","id":1018035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crying</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/431083-101-scion-story-hooks?p=1017935#post1017935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>175) </b>Everybody knows that kisses have magical properties, particularly the ability to break curses. The kiss of a princess can undo metamorphosis spells, true love's first kiss can undo sleep or mind control spells, etc...<br /> <br /> The thing that's puzzling you is that last you checked, you were slowly dying from a curse and the only other person in this cave with you is your rival. How come you feel better now..?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Tsundere rival! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>176) </b>The Muspel and the Jotun, two races who seem like they shouldn't even exist within the same city as each other have done the unthinkable, they had a kid together! Now, a brand new species of giant has been brought into the Nine Realms, with skin as strong as iron and blood like boiling water. The fate of this newborn &quot;steam giant&quot; is unknown this early in its development. But the Ragnarok claims the giants will destroy the Norse pantheon, so they don't trust the little abomination just on principle. Still, there may be some way to turn this to their advantage. Loki may be a god now, but he was originally born a fire giant. Perhaps the gods can accomplish something similar with this one?<br /> <br /> Long story short, Odin is sending you to kidnap a newborn giant with unexplored powers who is being guarded by both a Jotun mother and a Muspel father. It also doesn't help that they are constantly surrounded by both fire and frost giants who anxiously want to get a look at the new hybrid. <i>Good luck with that!</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 12-16-2016, 08:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T22:45:53-08:00","id":1021851,"title":"","content":"<b>177) </b>Because of you and your Band's exploits, Zeus himself has an important mission for you, one that concerns the very Fate of the World --<br /> <br /> -- just kidding. He's arranging for a passionate tryst with the newest beauty to charge his thunderbolt, and he wants <i>you guys</i> to play lookout (and to distract Hera, if it comes to that).<br /> <br /> This is exactly the kind of quest that can't any get worse, right? Well, considering Zeus's prospective mistress <i>du jour</i> is a goddess from another pantheon...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12628,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12628-yukikaze","user":"yukikaze","date":". 12-25-2016, 09:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12628-yukikaze","name":"yukikaze","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T17:24:22-08:00","id":1023496,"title":"","content":"<b>178)</b> So, you know how the French government has been kind of an asshole? Tracking down Scions, capturing them and shipping them off to... somewhere, killing the ones who resist, stuff like that? Well, the President of France was just on television with his family, including his famously beautfiul wife and daughter. His famously beautiful wife and daughter who you can very clearly see are Harpies. You think you just figured out whats happening...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12300,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","user":"Crying","date":". 12-29-2016, 04:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","name":"Crying","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12300_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T19:18:34-08:00","id":1023544,"title":"","content":"<b>179)</b> You found yourself singing &quot;Mr. Sandman&quot; to yourself last night after getting the song stuck in your head for a couple hours. When it finally went away, you didn't think anything more of it until the next morning when you woke up to find a stranger laying naked in your bed with you. Even worse, they appear to match the description of the man you were asking for in the song, and they seem <i>very convinced</i> that you are supposed to spend the rest of your nights together!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T20:47:22-08:00","id":1023567,"title":"","content":"180) Gobekli Tepe, in Turkey, is possibly the oldest religious site in existence, her people a nomadic Neolithic culture lost to the ages. It is an archaeological wonder, a UNESCO World heritage site, and as of last Wednesday, the subject of about two dozen young Scions' dreams every single night since. Mankind has forgotten the gods once worshiped on this lonely Anatolian hill, but they - primordial animals all, but especially hungry vultures - have merely slept beneath they earth, and are no longer content to be relics of the past; they were dead for thousands of years before the youngest of the Netjer drew breath, and the world is not that which they remember.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T21:54:48-08:00","id":1023587,"title":"","content":"<b>181) </b>While at a party involving 400-proof nectar and Brazilian-style barbecued S\u00e6hr\u00edmnir, the trickster gods of several pantheons decided it would <i>fun</i> to see their Scions do some competitive thievery. And not the ISO-standard priceless artworks or artifacts from museums, oh no. Presidential seals, nuclear launch codes, the deepest and darkest contents of parliamentary and senatorial safes... pickpocketing these, and the potential for upwelling chaos, this is those trickster-deities' idea of <i>fun</i>.<br /> <br /> And if you're not one of the Scions &quot;honored&quot; with participation in the Thievery Games, you're one of the Scions tasked with damage control.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12628-yukikaze","name":"yukikaze","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T16:15:25-08:00","id":1024540,"title":"","content":"<b>182)</b> The good news is that the dictator of <b>[INSERT COUNTRY HERE]</b> has been overthrown. The bad news is that the Scion who did it installed themselves as the new ruler afterwards. They claim that they'll turn the country to democracy once they've &quot;sorted things out&quot; but you're not so sure you believe that. Besides, you're pretty sure that, even if that is their plan, if they don't 'abdicate the throne' soon then they'll start picking up Fatebonds which will make it hard to follow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","name":"Crying","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12300_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T00:20:11-08:00","id":1024649,"title":"","content":"<b>183) </b>Loki is FREE! (Seriously, it's amazing how much he gets around, despite being trapped in the cave with the snake with the dripping poison fangs.) And he's stolen one of the great treasures from another pantheon and hidden it under a &quot;big W.&quot;<br /> <br /> Yes, he's seen <i>It's a Mad, Mad, Mad, Mad World</i>. No, it's not under <i>that</i> big W. You didn't really think it was gonna be that easy, did you...?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12628-yukikaze","name":"yukikaze","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T02:36:43-08:00","id":1024686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>yukikaze</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/431083-101-scion-story-hooks?p=1024649#post1024649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>183) </b>Loki is FREE! (Seriously, it's amazing how much he gets around, despite being trapped in the cave with the snake with the dripping poison fangs.) And he's stolen one of the great treasures from another pantheon and hidden it under a &amp;quot;big W.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> Yes, he's seen <i>It's a Mad, Mad, Mad, Mad World</i>. No, it's not under <i>that</i> big W. You didn't really think it was gonna be that easy, did you...?</div> </div> </div> </div>Its Washington dc l?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T11:26:21-08:00","id":1024852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/431083-101-scion-story-hooks?p=1024686#post1024686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Its Washington dc l?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not quite:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/It%27s_a_Mad,_Mad,_Mad,_Mad_World\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/da/It%27s_a_Mad%2C_Mad%2C_Mad%2C_Mad_World_%281963%29_theatrical_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/It%27s_a_Mad,_Mad,_Mad,_Mad_World\" target=\"_blank\"> It's a Mad, Mad, Mad, Mad World - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/It%27s_a_Mad,_Mad,_Mad,_Mad_World\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/It%27s_a_Mad,_Mad,_Mad,_Mad_World </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12628-yukikaze","name":"yukikaze","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T17:02:06-08:00","id":1026226,"title":"","content":"<b>184)</b> You have a half brother, a mortal who's known about your Scion heritage for nearly as long as you have. And while they outwardly put up a front of being supportive of you, your divine senses could easily tell they were always jealous of your, quite literally, god given talents. It's a sibling's job to compete with each other for dominance, but that was an impossible rivalry, given your backgrounds. That is until recently, however, when your brother announced their debut in a grandiose fashion. Somehow, they managed to get in touch with the giants and have been drinking heavy quantities of their blood in the hopes of being able to keep pace with you. And now, their binge drinking has paid off; your sibling has become a full fledged giant, a cyclops!<br /> <br /> Now, they're on some kind of power trip, eager to prove they can be just as great a hero as you. Better, even, since they've been studying how you work and think you're a bit too sloppy. Unfortunately, Fate isn't content to just let this turn of events go unnoticed. It seems that Zeus is not pleased with your sibling, nobody should consider themselves equal to the children of Olympus, especially not some wannabe Scion turned Titanspawn.<br /> <br /> The king of the Gods wants your brother in chains, enslaved in some forge under Olympus and forced to produce lightning bolts for use against Gaia's armies. But even though you and your brother have been rivals, there hasn't actually been a case of bad blood between the two of you. You have no reason to hate them, other than the fact they aren't pretty enough to meet Olympus' standards of quality.<br /> <br /> So now you face a quandary; do you obey your king and enslave your own brother for the crime of doing what comes naturally to siblings, or do you attempt to persuade Zeus to give them a lighter sentence in hopes of preventing your rivalry from escalating into something more violent?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 01-16-2017, 11:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T18:26:51-08:00","id":1026252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/431083-101-scion-story-hooks?p=1026226#post1026226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>184)</b> You have half brother, a mortal who's known about your Scion heritage for nearly as long as you have. And while they outwardly put up a front of being supportive of you, your divine senses could easily tell they were always a jealous of your, quite literally, god given talents. It's a sibling's job to compete with each other for dominance, but that an impossible rivalry, given your backgrounds. That is until recently, however, when your brother announced their debut in a grandiose fashion. Somehow, they managed to get in touch with the giants and have been drinking heavy quantities of their blood in the hopes of being able to keep pace with you. And now, their binge drinking has paid off, your sibling has become a full fledged giant, a cyclops!<br /> <br /> Now, they're on some kind of power trip, eager to prove they can be just as great a hero as you. Better, even, since they've been studying how you work and think you're a bit too sloppy. Unfortunately, Fate isn't content to just let this turn of events go unnoticed. It seems that Zeus is not pleased with your sibling, nobody should consider themselves equal to the children of Olympus, especially not some wannabe Scion turned Titanspawn.<br /> <br /> The king of the Gods wants your brother in chains, enslaved in some forge under Olympus and forced to produce lightning bolts for use against Gaia's armies. But even though you and your brother have been rivals, there hasn't actually been a case of bad blood between the two of you. You have no reason to hate them, other than the fact they aren't pretty enough to meet Olympus' standards of quality.<br /> <br /> So now you face a quandary; do you obey your king and enslave your own brother for the crime of doing what comes naturally to siblings, or do you attempt to persuade Zeus to give them a lighter sentence in hopes of preventing your rivalry from escalating into something more violent?</div> </div> </div> </div>How about asking for asylum or more to another Pantheon? I know one God who'd want to help just to one up Zeus, especially to help an giant. He has the title of [i]Giant's son[i] after all","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T20:14:57-08:00","id":1026285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/431083-101-scion-story-hooks?p=1026252#post1026252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about asking for asylum or more to another Pantheon? I know one God who'd want to help just to one up Zeus, especially to help an giant. He has the title of [i]Giant's son[i] after all</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I assume you're referring to Loki?<br /> <br /> And that might be possible... of course, then you'd have to deal with the consequences of A) trying to go behind Zeus' back, and B) doing so with one of the most devious Gods in all mythology!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T20:26:06-08:00","id":1026292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/431083-101-scion-story-hooks?p=1026285#post1026285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I assume you're referring to Loki?<br /> <br /> And that might be possible... of course, then you'd have to deal with the consequences of A) trying to go behind Zeus' back, and B) doing so with one of the most devious Gods in all mythology!</div> </div> </div> </div>Also,there's the risky option: you could walk right up Zeus face and say &quot;you're becoming just like your father&quot; that'd leave an impact","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T21:16:57-08:00","id":1026304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/431083-101-scion-story-hooks?p=1026292#post1026292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also,there's the risky option: you could walk right up Zeus face and say &quot;you're becoming just like your father&quot; that'd leave an impact</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> He used Hera for target practice the one time she tried to take her anger out on him... I wouldn't recommend trying that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T21:28:02-08:00","id":1026310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/431083-101-scion-story-hooks?p=1026304#post1026304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> He used Hera for target practice the one time she tried to take her anger out on him... I wouldn't recommend trying that.</div> </div> </div> </div>The gist of this idea it's not insulting his pride, it's making him afraid. He knows for a fact Fate decreed he will be overthrown and Killed. It stands to reason that the more he acts like the previously overthrown rulers, the more likely it will happen to hime too. It's only logical","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T22:34:18-08:00","id":1026333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/431083-101-scion-story-hooks?p=1026310#post1026310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The gist of this idea it's not insulting his pride, it's making him afraid. He knows for a fact Fate decreed he will be overthrown and Killed. It stands to reason that the more he acts like the previously overthrown rulers, the more likely it will happen to hime too. It's only logical</div> </div> </div> </div>The more he acts like the previous rulers, <i>and</i> the more he intentionally tries to not act like the previous rulers both would tighten Fate's noose around his neck. Greek Fate loves when you try to fight it, all you end up doing is walking closer to your Fated doom. Oedipus and Perseus are the big poster boys for, &quot;If you try to fight it, it will happen quicker than not.&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T23:17:54-08:00","id":1026351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/431083-101-scion-story-hooks?p=1026310#post1026310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The gist of this idea it's not insulting his pride, it's making him afraid. He knows for a fact Fate decreed he will be overthrown and Killed. It stands to reason that the more he acts like the previously overthrown rulers, the more likely it will happen to hime too. It's only logical</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ah, I see now.<br /> <br /> Come to think of it, I don't remember the previous two rulers of Olympus actually being outright killed... they were castrated, though. Which I don't think Zeus would be very pleased with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T09:00:46-08:00","id":1026550,"title":"","content":"You might be able to convince him that you now-cyclops brother could serve as a &quot;family retainer&quot;, allowing him to follow you around fulfilling his fatebound role as your rival while adhering to the spirit of the decree of not the letter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T16:21:06-08:00","id":1026751,"title":"","content":"<b>185)</b> In a world where Scion existence is openly recognized by the public, one corporation is dedicated to giving the average citizen peace of mind in these troubled times. Calling themselves Mythic Industries, they have begun to provide numerous services to the public that allow them to compete with the otherwise vastly superior Scions. Their goal, or so they claim, is to prevent the Scions from establishing a coup by using their divine powers to usurp control of the world governments.<br /> <br /> Except that mystically perceptive Scions had noticed multiple discrepancies in their alleged background. For one, Mythic Industries is a multi national corporation that just kind of appeared out of the blue all across the world. Secondly, their idea of balancing the threat Scions pose is to grant supernatural abilities to their customers. And finally, these supernatural abilities unanimously reflect the powers of various species of Titanspawn!<br /> <br /> That's right, Hundun, the greater Titan of Chaos is the one pulling Mythic Industries' strings. Somehow, they figured out a way to warp history and are now preying upon the fear, anger and outright jealousy caused by a world where the supernatural has gone mainstream. Through the use of the company, they have been twisting mortals into Titanspawn right under the noses of the Gods. All under the false pretense of maintaining balance and security in a world where some teenager with a knife is more powerful than an entire squad of armed police officers!<br /> <br /> <br /> He may be an ancient, primordial entity, but you have to admit that Hundun's plan was flawlessly executed. They've already branded themselves as the good guys in the public image, and laying siege to their corporation will immediately draw the scorn of billions of mortals who feel threatened by the existence of Scions. No, the only way to fix this damage is to recreate whatever power Hundun used to rewrite history and stop him from changing it in the first place. Unfortunately, none of the pantheons even thought such a feat was possible until now, which means your research has to start from scratch!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T16:36:34-08:00","id":1032987,"title":"","content":"<b>186) </b>Recently your Rival hasn't been much of a rival. They've fallen behind you in Legend and can't seem to catch up, so basically nothing they try to do challenges you anymore. You're simply better than them... and they know it. So they've been trying to find ways to screw with you that don't involve actually challenging you in something. It seems they've found one too; you've come home, wanting to visit your mortal parent, only for them to answer the door dressed in your mother's/father's dressing gown and seemingly nothing underneath.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","name":"Crying","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12300_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T20:28:59-08:00","id":1033117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crying</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/431083-101-scion-story-hooks?p=1032987#post1032987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>186) </b>Recently your Rival hasn't been much of a rival. They've fallen behind you in Legend and can't seem to catch up, so basically nothing they try to do challenges you anymore. You're simply better than them... and they know it. So they've been trying to find ways to screw with you that don't involve actually challenging you in something. It seems they've found one too; you've come home, wanting to visit your mortal parent, only for them to answer the door dressed in your mother's/father's dressing gown and seemingly nothing underneath.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is why the various pantheons like to castrate their rivals...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T22:31:14-08:00","id":1033163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/431083-101-scion-story-hooks?p=1033117#post1033117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> This is why the various pantheons like to castrate their rivals...</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/6VZhSkREYBc\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/6VZhSkREYBc\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/6VZhSkREYBc\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/6VZhSkREYBc </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>187)</b> Terror on the high seas! Something seems to be terrorizing ships around the San Francisco Bay Area, but no one knows what, until one night when a traffic chopper catches grainy footage of -- Cipactli?!<br /> <br /> That's right, it looks like the primordial sea monster of Aztec mythology (or at least one of its children or servants) has decided to make life hard for the Bay Area. Time to go (Giant) Crocodile Hunting.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12628-yukikaze","name":"yukikaze","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T06:59:36-08:00","id":1033988,"title":"","content":"<b>188)</b> Something isn't right; natural disasters have been spontaneously occurring throughout the country. I don't mean they occur without reason, I mean one second everything is fine and then in an instant you're suddenly in the middle of a hurricane, or an earthquake, a flash flood, est. It would require an immense level of concentrated Chaos in order to perform a feat like this, and you can't think of anybody in recent memory capable of pulling that off.<br /> <br /> Oh wait... didn't you hear about a new Band consisting almost entirely of Tricksters emerging a few months ago?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T06:12:43-08:00","id":1035693,"title":"","content":"<b>189)</b> Thor is pretty good at acting. I mean, with some help from Loki he was able to convince a Jotun king that he was Freya, so that's hardly surprising. Nor is it surprising that he spends a good deal of his mortal life as an actor playing himself in a superhero movie.<br /> <br /> What is surprising is that Loki, who is currently supposed to be imprisoned in Helheim, managed to get onset to play himself in the next installment. Maybe you should look into this...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12300,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","user":"Crying","date":". 01-22-2017, 09:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","name":"Crying","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12300_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T08:44:06-08:00","id":1037861,"title":"","content":"<b>190)</b> VR gaming is becoming an increasingly popular trend of late, and one particular headset has been turning heads among the supernatural market. According to rumor, if you die 9 times within 6 minute intervals on the 3rd hour of playing, you're sucked into a pocket reality. One designed in the image of the game you were playing. The only (publicly) known way to escape is to finish the game without dying again, because the next time, it's going to be permanent! Despite this, some young and impressionable beings continue to buy the headset in hopes of living out their favorite gaming series in real life, not fully comprehending the consequences of their actions until it's too late.<br /> <br /> As for for the unusual number sequence in getting the ritual to work, well the logo for the headset's manufacturer is a grinning fox...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":".  Edited the numbers, because I suck at math! 02-14-2017, 07:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T02:30:34-08:00","id":1048640,"title":"","content":"<b>191)</b> It probably seemed like a good idea at the time. Then again, a lot of things do when the Handsome Monkey King is on his fourth barrel of sake. The Japanese were being so hospitable, and he really wanted to show people he wasn't as selfish as he used to be! So why not give them a new hero? One that, conveniently, already has a cult following to drum up some worship. Well, turns out bringing Hatsune Miku to life as a Scion may have come across wrong, since now she's <i>his</i>\u200b Scion and the Shen are being accused of muscling in on Kami territory. Because nobody really expects Sun Wukong to clean up his own mess (or particularly wants him to try) you've been sent to try and deal with this before a war breaks out.<br /> <br /> <b>192)</b> Hermes, Dionysus and Hephaestus all walk into a bar. It sounds like the setup to a bad joke, but after an event involving enough alcohol to poison a small country, &quot;Demons&quot; by Imagine Dragons playing on the radio and the destruction and immediate divine reconstruction of a bridge in Dublin, it instead resulted in a new Scion made of pure, enchanted gold, infused with power from each god and proclaimed the new Saint, Divine Herald and Immortal Representationer of the Theoi. Apparently some gods get their words muddled when sufficiently drunk. As always happens when any pantheon does anything the others are already racing to respond, and you've been chosen to defend the new Golden Boy from threats and challenges. Lucky you!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12689-creepyshutin","name":"CreepyShutIn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T04:48:03-08:00","id":1048672,"title":"","content":"<b>193)</b> It's official, the moon landing was fake. The technology used at the time was too experimental and to be honest, mankind didn't really know what they were doing. But now, decades later, the government is secretly trying to plan a secondary attempt, one that will put a man on the moon for real! Unfortunately, the various moon deities are opposed to the idea of mortals showing up unannounced and planting a flag on their front lawn. They've contacted you to sabotage the space program and ensure that mortals remember to stick to their own planetoid.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>194)</b> When hearing the word 'demon,' most westerners instantly think of the most evil creatures in existence. Well it turns out that quite a large number of demons in the east are perfectly capable of civilized behavior, and they've decided that they would like to debunk the negative stereotypes held against them. They've started to migrate over seas, bringing along their best and their brightest to show that not all demons are monsters. Unfortunately, most people (who are aware of their presence) instantly leaped to conclusions and believe they are now under some sort of demonic invasion. Regardless of your beliefs on the subject, you've been contacted to act as mediator and sort this mess out before things turn into a cultural bloodbath!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T15:34:20-08:00","id":1051184,"title":"","content":"<b>195)</b> &quot;I don't care what the skalds wrote, we did NOT have sex! We were <b>wrestling.</b> There's a difference!&quot; Two rival Scions with a long history of heated arguments and conflict between them have found themselves in a strange predicament. During their last confrontation, in which they found themselves locked in hand to hand combat while attempting to strangle the life out of each other, one of them somehow got the other one pregnant and now they're fated to give birth to a Giant who will grow up to be an absurdly powerful warrior because he was literally conceived in battle. Nobody knows how this happened, but the two Scions involved are pointing fingers at the skalds and priests who misconstrued their battle as a metaphor for some hard core sex. Neither one of them is ready to be a parent, especially not for each other's child. But the Norns have warned that terminating it will piss off Fate, so they've turned to you for assistance.<br /> <br /> <br /> ( props to anybody who wants to take a crack at what the skald's poem might be. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 02-02-2018, 01:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T19:41:47-08:00","id":1051319,"title":"","content":"<b>196)</b> It was a childish wish, made out of ignorance. Not long ago you (or perhaps a member of the band) performed a service for the Kami and they offered to grant their servant one wish as a reward. Without properly thinking of the consequences, they wished to become &quot;stronger than the strong,&quot; believing they would simply receive a divine boost in strength. Unfortunately, that exact phrase has a very specific meaning among the Kami, and now their servant has been transformed into an Oni! They got what they wanted, their strength now far surpasses any mortal man or woman's, but now they're in the body of a Japanese demon, and their human personality is dwindling in favor of one befitting the Titan Spawn. Unless you find a way to reverse the wish, they will eventually lose their original self and become a true demon. Unfortunately, the Kami responsible for granting the wish decided to leave immediately afterward, and you don't know how to contact them!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T12:38:59-08:00","id":1052699,"title":"","content":"197) Wonderful. One of your rivals took a civilian close to you hostage. The demand is... rust from the signature weapon of another scion? What the actual... ?!<br /> Turns out, said scion wounded the rival, and that rust is the only way to heal the terrible festering wound. Also, the &quot;medicine&quot; must be procured before the sun sets, or else. The rival is not a bad person, but they are desperate and in pain. Good luck.<br /> <br /> 198) For one reason or another, you are temporarily tasked with looking after the moognificent wish-granting cow Kamadhenu. <br /> How many attempts to steal her, take her by force, or just plain demand her as a gift can you fend off? Because there will be many.<br /> In other news, do resist the urge to exploit the poor beast yourself. She needs some rest, you know. Vasishtha will know if something wrong happens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5530-xanthias","name":"Xanthias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T10:59:52-08:00","id":1053325,"title":"","content":"<b>199)</b> Well, son of a bitch; it seems that a bunch of mortals thought they could artificially turn themselves into Scions, via the Bloodborne method of infusing mortals with the blood of the old gods. Unfortunately in this case, 'old gods' refers to the Greater Titans! Somehow, they managed to get their hands on genetic materials from these primordial beings and have been conducting blasphemous, inhumane experiments with them. They believe that their work will grant mortals power akin to those of the gods, and elevate their status in the World. Instead, the only thing their work has managed to do is mutate their test subjects into monstrous Titan Spawn, destroying their human personalities in the process as they rapidly succumb to corruption. Most people would call it quits after the first batch of failures, but these mortals are so obsessed with their mission that they have degenerated into radical fanaticism, no longer having the capacity to discern success from failure!<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>200)</b> You've always wanted to vacation somewhere exotic, but never quite had the time or the money to do so. It always remained a coveted dream in the back of your mind, though, and when your father, Loki appeared before you with enough first class plane tickets for you and your entire band to go sight seeing, you were overjoyed. Unfortunately, Loki failed to mention that the vacation spot was not located on earth. Hell, it's not even in this plane of reality; it's located in one of 6 of the 9 realms (Hellheim, Midgard, and Asgard being off limits). To make matters worse, your tickets were for one way trips, which means you're stuck in this new world unless you can scrounge up the money for a ride back home. And oh, what a shame, but Midgard currency doesn't work here!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 11-18-2018, 12:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T22:48:24-08:00","id":1056995,"title":"","content":"<b>201)</b> The revitalization of Scions to the World has caused a turning point in the war, and now the Titans find themselves in need of reinforcements if they are to gain the upper hand again. They've decided the best way to obtain them is to start breeding. But no ordinary machination of the Titans will provide suitable offspring for what the Titans require. They don't need rank and file Titanspawn, they need monsters powerful enough to shake the very heavens where the Gods hold court. What they need is Typhon, the father of all monsters, and his mate, Echidna. But they've been imprisoned since the end of the first war, or were presumed dead thanks to divine propaganda. <br /> <br /> But the Titans believe they may have located the 'grave' sites where these unfathomable monsters have remained trapped for eons. And after thousands of years being sealed off from each other, Typhon and Echidna are undoubtedly pent up and eager to get back to business. Somebody needs to mobilize the defenses and prevent the Titans from unleashing a second Age of Monsters upon the unsuspecting World!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-02T17:40:29-07:00","id":1099697,"title":"","content":"<b>202)</b> It was a popular tradition in ancient Egypt for the next generation of pharaohs to erase the names of their predecessors from public records and edit their names in their place. In doing so, future generations were credited with the deeds of the past. Now, one of their Scions has resurrected this ancient practice, stealing the Legend of fallen Scions of Egypt and absorbing it for their own. Their goal is to catapult themselves to godhood by taking credit for the deeds of others, and there is evidence to suggest it might actually work. Unfortunately, their actions have begun to spark tensions of civil unrest and infighting among the Pesedjet's children who think they can steal credit for other people's work. This ambitious Scion must be stopped and in a public fashion so as to send a message to the rest that a civil war during a time of invasion will not be tolerated.<br /> <br /> Thankfully, this is a recent occurrence and they haven't yet gathered the momentum to be a major threat. But who knows how much longer that will last?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-03T19:35:06-07:00","id":1146532,"title":"","content":"<b>203)</b> A Scion of Heru has invented a series of surveillance equipment which isn't fooled by supernatural attempts at trickery and interference. Realizing the strategic value of his inventions, the gods have commissioned him to work on a spy satellite which will allow them to locate and monitor any supernatural being in the World, no matter how carefully hidden they think they are. Unfortunately, they're not the only ones who came up with the idea, and now Aten has dispatched their zealots to convert the Scion over to their side, where the Titan will have the means to hunt down every pocket of resistance on the planet, no matter where they try to hide.<br /> <br /> As fellow Scions, your band has been placed on security detail, and it's your job to make sure Heru's son completes his work on the satellite without being turned into a brainwashed slave. After that, it's a simple matter of ensuring the satellite makes it into space without exploding, or some other equally disastrous occurrence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 10-03-2017, 10:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-03T20:07:29-07:00","id":1146538,"title":"","content":"<b>204)</b> The worst fears of the gods have come true: a Scion loyal to the titans has created an astra that, when wielded by its intended recipient, is powerful enough to annihilate all resistance and kill the mightiest gods. As it is intended for Apep, the serpent that would devour the sun, the gods have realized that the World is in a spot of trouble.<br /> <br /> Worse yet, this astra cannot be destroyed except by one entity: Typhon, the most feared of all Greek god-monsters. The magic that makes the weapon so powerful requires at least one critical weakness, and so its maker chose its destroyer to be the one entity that has absolutely no reason whatsoever to do the gods any favors.<br /> <br /> Fortunately, Odin has a plan.<br /> <br /> The vain Scion has secretly called together a grand convocation of titans, their servants and their spawn to unveil the new weapon and gain eternal glory in the eyes of their patrons. This little soiree is the only time the astra will be taken from its hiding place before being delivered to Apep; if the gods want to get the astra, this is the time to do it.<br /> <br /> Odin's plan is simple: assemble a team of the World's finest thieves, con artists, and adventurers to pull the greatest combination heist/confidence scheme in history. They're going to steal the astra from under the noses of some of the most dangerous beings in the universe, and then trick what might be <i>the</i> most dangerous being in the universe into destroying it.<br /> <br /> If they pull it off, the tale will never be forgotten. If they fail, the sun gets eaten and the World dies. No pressure.<br /> <br /> I call it: <b>Odin's Eleven</b>.<br /> <br /> Edit: Yet more complexity might be added through the necessity of ensuring the titans cannot create another invincible astra. This would involve deceiving the smith-Scion into revealing the location of their research/power source/secret sauce, and then killing them. Naturally, this would have to be done during the heist itself, as the Scion is too clever to show their hand before unveiling the astra.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":175,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","user":"Prometheus878","date":". 10-04-2017, 02:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-04T10:12:56-07:00","id":1146711,"title":"","content":"<b>205)</b> The owl, a bird of prey revered for its wisdom and ability to move about in perfect silence at night. The mice and shrews are right to be terrified of them when they're on the hunt. But when the national forest becomes home to a Nemean owl, campers start to get picked off in the middle of the night before they even know what hit them! Hunting in the forest is illegal under federal law, which is unfortunate for you, because you've just been tasked with slaying the beast!<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>206) </b>A minor forge deity has decided to bring his imagination to life by crafting suits of relic armor to aid others in the fight against the Titans. Unfortunately, this craftsman seems to be a bit of a pervert, and the suits he makes for females are so revealing that they are deemed unfit to be called 'armor.' Yet, somehow, they seem to confer some sort of magical protection upon their wearers, regardless of how much (or how little) they seem to be wearing. One of your bandmates is the child of a female deity who wants to set up a commission, but demands the finished product is something more appropriately modest for her to wear in public.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, the craftsman views his creations as a passionate work of art and insists that he be allowed to create the piece in the style to which he is accustomed. Neither side appears willing to relent their side of the argument, and the flustered goddess is too proud to accept rejection from a deity of lesser station, so she refuses to simply commission another smith to complete the armor for her. Your band needs to find some way to resolve the argument, because she keeps bringing it up at every opportunity, which is really starting to embarrass your bandmate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-06T00:23:20-07:00","id":1147337,"title":"","content":"If you want to get a little meta about Scion edition changes...<br /> <br /> <b>207)</b> The war has been raging for years. For decades. But now there's a feeling in the air. Both sides can sense it. There's a change coming. A change in power, and maybe even a change in the war itself and what it's all about. Truth to tell it's got everyone from the mightiest Greek god to the most epic layered Titan-aspect kind of freaked out. So there's a new arms race, as the newest Scion band competes with a band of Titanspawn to figure out what the changes are and how to be prepared and take advantage of the sudden shift before the other side can.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2608-squee","name":"Squee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2608_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-09T08:08:29-07:00","id":1148308,"title":"","content":"<b>208)</b> What happens when you apply the Typhonian template to a Megaladon? Well, that's what Cipactli wanted to find out, and now we've got a shark of such magnitude that battle ships look like bite sized snacks! They're currently rampaging throughout the seas and making life terrible for the various water deities who have to deal with this new &quot;Ultradon&quot; shark. Realizing they're in desperate need of backup, they've petitioned your band for support while they plan to launch a coordinated strike against this colossal Titanspawn!<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>209)</b> Something's happened to the Norse pantheon, causing all their personalities to become inverted! And for once, Loki doesn't seem to be the cause of this disruption, because the last time anybody saw him, he was hefting a battle axe in both hands and charging into battle like a valiant warrior! Thor, on the other hand, has become a bit of an egg head. Putting his hammer down and hitting the books to learn as much about sorcery and rune craft as he can get his hands on. Odin is being simultaneously more and less helpful than usual, as he's both a compassionate leader and yet he doesn't have access to the all knowing wisdom he's carried throughout the ages. Some speculate that it was a misguided attempt to circumvent the effects of Ragnarok by forcing the gods to adopt different callings, while others believe it is a trick intended to throw the pantheon into disarray while the giants marshal their forces. Fortunately, only the Norse seem to be affected by this predicament, which is why they decided to reach out to Scions of the other pantheons to find out what the hell's going on!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-09T09:30:20-07:00","id":1148328,"title":"","content":"210) &quot;And in local news, a riot broke out at the Heaven's Brew Tavern on 8th Street. The local tavern, specializing in homecrafted microbrews, reportedly suffered from several patrons suddenly flipping tables and breaking decorations. One of the rioters, whose identity will remain undisclosed pending investigation, claims that they were told to do so by Dionysus of the Theoi, as punishment for calling the tavern Heaven's Brew but serving what he called, quote, 'Lukewarm horse piss'. The head of the local Helenist church did not make any comments on whether or not this was the official stance of Dionysus, but did say that it would be unwise to make claims that you cannot back up.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-09T17:00:03-07:00","id":1148472,"title":"","content":"Origin Story<br /> <br /> <b>211)</b> <i>Who Wants to be a Scion:</i> One of the Gods is looking to patronize a mortal as their champion, but isn't quite sure who's most deserving of that honor. In order to find a worthy candidate, they've decided to hold a talent competition (the specifics of which are based on the deity in question). The winner will have the esteemed honor of becoming their new Scion, and a potential shot at godhood. It's a reward that many would be willing to kill for, as you quickly discover after being accepted into the competition!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-21T09:09:09-07:00","id":1151655,"title":"","content":"<b>212)</b> Your pantheon has organized a pizza party with a franchise who promises to make the delivery within a certain time limit, or it's free. Unfortunately, the franchise's reputation is quite stirling... almost Legendary, if you want to put it that way. The Gods usually don't have need for a financial income, and they were really banking on that free pizza delivery service to resolve the problem. That's where you come into the picture. They want you to delay the delivery man and cause him to miss the deadline. And they want you to do it in the most subtle way possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-25T20:01:17-07:00","id":1153017,"title":"","content":"<b>213)</b> A pair of married Scions didn't work out so well together and decide the best course of action is to get a divorce. As is typical in these situations, the court rules that the more financially secure party hand over roughly half their assets to their less stable partner in order to support their livelihood in the aftermath of the separation. Unfortunately, the court ordered <i>&quot;hand over your shit&quot;</i> goes so far as to include the ex's Relics, which they are not willing to surrender peacefully.<br /> <br /> Incensed by this refusal, they've requested your band to assist them in 'convincing' their ex to comply with the divorce settlement. At the same time, the offending party requests your aid in exacting revenge upon the one who ruined their life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-15T10:08:00-08:00","id":1159026,"title":"","content":"<b>214)</b> Rumours have been circulating that in an unprecedented display of teamwork, several pantheons' tricksters have been arranging a Grand Scheme which they're sure will cut the titans down to size. However, one of the tricksters is certain that one or more of the gods are skewing the plan to benefit them and has contacted your band to ask them to act as impartial observers to make sure no funny business is going on. And this totally isn't an elaborate plan to get a leg up themselves, no sir. And the band absolutely won't find themselves caught up in the Grand Scheme themselves...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13499-not-quite-yoda","name":"Not Quite Yoda","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T00:45:46-08:00","id":1161781,"title":"","content":"<b>215</b>) Your birthright, a possessed sword, has become one of your closest companions over the course of your adventures, possibly even your best friend - or, rather, the spirit inside your birthright has. You're very close with them, able to talk about anything and everything that's on your mind when you feel you need a discussion, but recently they've started behaving oddly. They've become more quiet, more reserved, more... distant. I'll leave it up to you to figure out the reason why, but I will give you one very big hint if you want it: <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> they're feelings for you might not be mere camaraderie...</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12300,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","user":"Crying","date":". 03-13-2020, 10:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","name":"Crying","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12300_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T11:55:14-08:00","id":1161933,"title":"","content":"216) &quot;<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">If you've ever taken a road trip through the Pacific Northwest, you've probably seen a bumper sticker for a place called Gravity Falls. It's not on any maps, and most people have never heard of it. Some people think it's a myth. But if you're curious, don't wait. Take a trip. Find it. It's out there somewhere in the woods, waiting.&quot;<br /> <br /> Admittedly, the stuff that goes down in Gravity Falls is, by and large, more mortal-tier and Hero-tier stuff, but fuck, that's what we'll have come game release. :P<br /> <br /> Required:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=645xo1qyLW8\" data-code=\"645xo1qyLW8\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/645xo1qyLW8/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div></span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T15:45:50-08:00","id":1161985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/431083-101-scion-story-hooks?p=1161933#post1161933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">216) <br /> <br /> Admittedly, the stuff that goes down in Gravity Falls is, by and large, more mortal-tier and Hero-tier stuff, but fuck, that's what we'll have come game release. :P<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You were saying....?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=w9DIYdslPhI\" data-code=\"w9DIYdslPhI\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/w9DIYdslPhI/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T16:28:44-08:00","id":1162003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/431083-101-scion-story-hooks?p=1161985#post1161985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> You were saying....?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=w9DIYdslPhI\" data-code=\"w9DIYdslPhI\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/w9DIYdslPhI/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>By and large. Bill is an outlier in many ways","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T00:51:09-08:00","id":1173172,"title":"","content":"<b>217) Competitive Eschatology</b><br /> <br /> <i>Its the end of the world. Which one? All of them.</i><br /> <br /> All of the end-times scenarios are taking place at once. Ragnarok, Frashokereti, the Flood, the Sermon of the Seven Suns, the end of the Kali Yuga, Sweeping Day, the Death of the Fifth Sun, the Fall of Olympus... some reports are even saying that its Judgement Day. Hell, there are even some non-mythical apocalyptic events going down too - more than a few nukes have been let fly durng all this chaos.<br /> <br /> There is some good news, however; everyone is trying to end the world, but they're trying to do it <i>their</i> way. Apep and Fenrir are fighting over who gets to devour the sun, Svarog and Brahman are arguing over which of them, exactly, gets to end this era and begin a new one, etc... The endbringers are actually putting more energy into fighting each other than they are in destroying Earth and, in this chaos, there's a chance - a slim chance, but a chance nonetheless - that creation can be saved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","name":"Crying","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12300_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-19T16:50:03-08:00","id":1177453,"title":"","content":"<b>218)</b> That tricksy Hephaestus is at it again, making a smaller version of Talos tasked to make more of itself before attacking Titans en masse. Unfortunately, he forgot to put an upper limit on the number of Taloses, and the Titans are sitting back as they slowly dismantle the World.<br /> <br /> <b>219) </b>A kappa has pulled a child into his river, which is not too unusual until you learn that this particular child was a changeling - and the changeling child of a local fairy queen, to boot. Can your band prevent all-out war between the local yokai and the sidhe?<br /> <br /> <b>220)</b> The unthinkable has happened - not only has a prominent god fallen, but by some quirk of fate they've passed on into the wrong underworld. You're tasked with finding where they've gone, braving the underworld's defences (which seem to have had some updates since the legends were written), and persuading the local deity that it's in their interest to give up the jewel of their collection.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13499-not-quite-yoda","name":"Not Quite Yoda","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-01T19:42:48-08:00","id":1181554,"title":"","content":"<b>221)</b> First, Cronus overthrew Uranus. Then, Zeus cast down Cronus in his turn. Fate would have it that one day, Zeus would have his throne taken from him by one of his children, for The Cycle of Violence is a prison that lets no victim go without a struggle.<br /> <br /> It is often forgotten that Zeus was considered a god of wisdom, foresight and just rulership by Hellenistic followers. Even Fate forgot this, but Zeus did not. He will not allow the world to be torn apart and his immortal soul thrown into Tartarus, by Jove! If he must surrender the throne, he shall do so on <i>his</i> terms.<br /> <br /> And so, he who delights in thunder has done the unthinkable: Zeus has announced his retirement. But the crown must rest on someone's head, and so Optimus Maximus has declared that whoever would succeed him must prove, before Heaven and the World beyond all doubt, that they are the Best and the Greatest.<br /> <br /> A grand test of Labors has been declared, a series of brutal tournaments and grueling tests. The contestants must prove their superiority to each other and to Zeus in order to inherit, and no god or scion will pull their punches in this greatest of all trials.<br /> <br /> Do you have what it takes to claim the Thunderbolt? Or perhaps, will you play the kingmaker? Whatever will happen, whoever wins, Glory will fall upon those who take part like rain in a storm. <i>To the Strongest!</i><br /> <br /> Edit: I've toyed with the idea of Zeus being a villain in this story, arranging the contest to discover who were his biggest threats. I decided against this because it would be cliche, and Jupiter being wise enough to quit while he's ahead would be more surprising to a modern audience. Besides, possessing positive leadership qualities and forethought does not preclude him from being an antagonistic jerk in other ways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":175,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","user":"Prometheus878","date":". 02-02-2018, 01:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-06T14:49:45-08:00","id":1183049,"title":"","content":"<b>222)</b> Vault B:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5pb6Ty2uuk8\" data-code=\"5pb6Ty2uuk8\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/5pb6Ty2uuk8/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-07T14:04:17-08:00","id":1183374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/431083-101-scion-story-hooks?p=1183049#post1183049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>222)</b> Vault B:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5pb6Ty2uuk8\" data-code=\"5pb6Ty2uuk8\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/5pb6Ty2uuk8/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Indiana Jones and the Secret of the Golden Temple<br /> <br /> Alternatively:<br /> <br /> Uncharted 5: The Vault of Vishnu<br /> <br /> *ADVENTURE INTENSIFIES*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-15T17:50:17-07:00","id":1227788,"title":"","content":"223) How do you &quot;misplace&quot; a Mantle?!<br /> <br /> It seems ridiculous, but that's what Dionysus claims happened. Looks aside, he's a very old god, and like many old gods he used to be very different. He hasn't even thought about his oldest Mantles in years, so imagine his shock to find out he doesn't have one of them anymore. A bit of searching (and quiet pleading with Djehuti, since he doesn't want the other Theoi to find out about this) turned up a teenage boy in southern Germany calling himself &quot;Jaeger.&quot; After seemingly dying to a vicious bear attack, young Jaeger has returned to his hometown, good as new, and started gathering followers. Stories of debauchery and rampant drug use were just the start; now people are disappearing and Jaeger's cult is getting a reputation for unhinged behavior.<br /> <br /> Dionysus may spend nearly all of his time drunk, but he's sharp enough to see how this could end badly for him. So he has a simple mission for a team of Scions: Kill the nascent god, retrieve his Mantle, and make sure no evidence remains to link this to him. And it goes without saying that if they tell anyone they will all be turned into ferns.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12689,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12689-creepyshutin","user":"CreepyShutIn","date":". 07-03-2018, 03:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12689-creepyshutin","name":"CreepyShutIn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-25T10:43:47-07:00","id":1230048,"title":"","content":"Simple concept: Campaign based around stylized versions of the Twelve Labors of Hercules. Add complications so that each labor lasts for several months of playing time. The players start as Origin level characters and each completed labor gives them 1 point of Legend. That gets them all the way up to Level 12 gods.<br /> <br /> Of course, I don't mean taking the labors literally. Demigods and up could probably finish the actual labors with a snap of their fingers. Also, players will soon figure out what path Fate has put them on, so you have to change things up. Still, it's a straightforward skeleton to use as a starting point for a campaign. ---Jim","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4310-jagardner","name":"jagardner","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-02T14:11:10-07:00","id":1231928,"title":"","content":"<b>Action Thriller:<br /> <br /> 225)</b> Somebody has kidnapped the Easter Bunny and is threatening them with bodily harm unless the Gods of Fertility agree to pay their ransom. It looks like your band just got contracted to perform a search and rescue operation!<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Stone Age Setting:</b><br /> <br /> <b>226)</b> It's been a while since the Gods performed a major act of creation and they've decided to shake off the rust by creating a new planet, capable of sustaining intelligent life. The only problem is that they need people to 'beta test' this new planet and prove to the Gods that it's suitable for their desires. That's when random Scions all over the world begin receiving letters saying that they've been selected for an all expense paid trip, courtesy of their respective pantheons.<br /> <br /> It isn't until after they arrive on this new world that they discover the ecosystem is completely untouched by modern civilization, and teeming with prehistoric monsters!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 07-02-2018, 05:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-04T07:17:11-07:00","id":1232363,"title":"","content":"<b>Theoi Setting:</b><br /> <br /> <b>227)</b> Poseidon has grown sick of mortals carelessly polluting his once beautiful seas and has decided to take the earth's water supply hostage. Just to rub it in their faces, he's moving it to planet Neptune, as if to remind everybody of who the seas truly belong to. Unfortunately, the sea is Poseidon's domain, and without its presence, the God of the Seas has no authority on the planet. Which means that both his cultists and any Scion connected to Poseidon can't harness their gifts properly, if they can even harness them at all. It looks like somebody is going to have to negotiate with Poseidon on humanity's behalf and convince him to return the earth's water, preferably before everybody dies from dehydration!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-27T13:32:14-07:00","id":1257639,"title":"","content":"<b>228)</b> An archaeologist found the Book of the Dead and managed to translate it, and now is journeying down to Duat to try and bring the dead back for money.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24271-froggo","name":"Froggo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24271_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-29T21:00:56-07:00","id":1258102,"title":"","content":"<b>229) </b>The Alusi Pantheon of the Igbo breaks into the Overworld and demands representation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24271-froggo","name":"Froggo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24271_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-13T17:09:46-08:00","id":1267140,"title":"","content":"<b>230)</b> An enchanted forest has given rise to hyper intelligent animals that have gradually learned to imitate the ways of medieval, human society. While the magic of the forest keeps them hidden from the outside world, some of the Gods have taken an interest in the intelligent wildlife, and graciously selected a few lucky members to become Scions. But while some might view such intervention as a time for celebration, others have reacted with fear. One of these bestial Scions fancies themselves the undisputed ruler of the forest, and has begun ruthlessly oppressing any creatures who attempt to defy them. <br /> <br /> As a fellow Scion with access to your own assortment of powers, you naturally find yourselves in their crosshairs as either a potential ally, or a threat to their dominance. And they don't have a lot of patience when it comes to potential rivals choosing which side of the war they'll stand on!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-11T18:15:11-07:00","id":1317922,"title":"","content":"<b>ARISE FROM YOUR GRAVE</b><br /> <br /> <b>231)</b> The beautiful, resource-rich mediterranean island state of Helenos has changed hands hundreds of times throughout the centuries. Now, many fear it is about to see its most brutal confrontation yet.<br /> <br /> Nestled in the midst of the Aegean sea, Helenos is caught between the ambitions of two budding neo-feudalist democratic empires. The Achaean League, led by aggressively ambitious Agatha Atreides, and the Trojan Alliance, guided by proudly paternal Prestor Priamos, seek to place their political candidate of choice into the island's presidential office, bringing its gorgeous environs, surprisingly large population, and bountiful well of natural resources under their sway.<br /> <br /> The League enjoys the favor of the common people. Its candidate, Agatha Atreides' younger brother Morgan, has won the heart of the average citizen through his irreproachable conduct, quiet competence, and genuine zeal for good governance. The majority of Helenian voters are convinced that Morgan has the best interests of the common man at heart, and it comes as little surprise that he won the popular election by a landslide. If only the story had ended there.<br /> <br /> While the citizenry of Helenos were making their own choice, their &quot;leadership&quot; was making theirs. The corruption and incompetence of the Helenian government has been an open disgrace for decades, and the man and woman on the street are sick to death of it. Morgan Atreides stood on a platform of profound, widespread reforms, and seems to be that rarest of creatures: a politician that will keep his promises. In the face of having their numerous crimes and failures exposed and suitably punished, local officials have instead pushed hard for the ascendance of the infamous Phillip Priamos.<br /> <br /> Long-lost son of Prestor Priamos, Phillip is an infamous globe-trotting playboy, gambler, and &quot;adventurer.&quot; Having rediscovered his true parents after a decade of searching, Phillip seems to have taken an interest in the &quot;family business&quot; of rulership, and has picked Helenos as his domain of choice (mostly, it seems, because of its value as a tourist destination). While Phillip might be great at entertaining vapid celebrities and jaded elites at parties, he's not quite so good at winning the hearts and minds of people who actually work for a living. Naturally, when Phillip realized he couldn't get by with empty platitudes and shallow charisma, he resorted to outright cheating.<br /> <br /> And so, despite Morgan Atreides' overwhelming victory, the Helenian government has installed Phillip Priamos as president anyway. For the Helenian people, this is the last straw. It's revolution or bust.<br /> <br /> War looms on the horizon, public protest and civil strife growing daily. The two powers marshal their forces, summon their allies and vassals, and prepare for a potentially long and deadly conflict. Both cannot control the Aegean. One must conquer.<br /> <br /> Enter the heroes. The two nations call for all the aid they can get, mortal and divine, and the Scions have a choice to make. Who do they side with and why? Is it too late for peace? And if war must happen, then how far will the heroes go to achieve their goals?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":175,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","user":"Prometheus878","date":". 06-12-2019, 04:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-16T03:17:20-07:00","id":1318824,"title":"","content":"<b>232)</b> It seems that a gang of adolescent thieves have taken to using parkour as a means of carrying out their more extravagant pilfering. At first, it wasn't anything the band needed to concern itself with. But after several of the thieves are discovered attempting to steal from them, Fate itself takes an interest in their development. It seems that these free running bandits have unwittingly become a clan of amateur ninjas, and they're starting to manifest abilities which exceed those of the average mortal!<br /> <br /> Can you find the grand master of their organization and put a stop to their crime spree, or will the city fall prey to a wave of super powered burglars and pickpockets?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 06-16-2019, 06:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-20T10:15:44-07:00","id":1319751,"title":"","content":"<b>233)</b> A series of grisly murders have started over the last several weeks, with police investigators being utterly appalled by the state the bodies were found in. It seems that one of the local satyrs has developed a passion for killing lately, and decided to try their hand at being at becoming an urban Legend. Unsure about how to deal with such a creature, the chief has reached out to the band to help resolve the situation. Preferably before this horned maniac manages to kill everybody who walks the streets at night!<br /> <br /> <b>234)</b> The sports entertainment industry is locked in a debate over whether or not centaurs should be allowed to compete in horse races, as well as whether or not they require a jockey to ride them across the finish line. Tensions are building between the young athletes who want to compete in the races, and the sponsors who refuse to legitimize them. Somebody needs to step in and bring about a satisfying resolution to the situation. But that somebody would need the charisma of the Gods to not have this spiral into an all out conflict between the two sides. Luckily for you, Scions just so happen to possess some measure of their patron's magnetic charm!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-07T18:42:27-07:00","id":1322864,"title":"","content":"<b>235)</b> A Goblin Slayer inspired Denizen story, in which the narrative revolves around a group of background characters going about their lives while the Scions are saving the world off camera.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}